rulings: ["[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.'}]", '[{\'date\': \'2009-10-01\', \'text\': "If the targeted permanent is an illegal target by the time Into the Roil resolves, the entire spell doesn\'t resolve. You don\'t draw a card."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'An ability that triggers when a player casts a kicked spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell. It resolves even if that spell is countered.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If the target nonland permanent is an illegal target by the time Into the Roil tries to resolve, the spell doesn\'t resolve. You don\'t draw a card if it was kicked."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If you copy a kicked spell, the copy is also kicked. If a card or token enters the battlefield as a copy of a permanent that\'s already on the battlefield, the new permanent isn\'t kicked, even if the original was."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can\'t kick it."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'Kicker represents an optional additional cost that you may choose to pay as you cast the spell. A spell cast with that additional cost paid is "kicked."\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Some instant or sorcery spells require alternative or additional targets if they\'re kicked. You ignore these targeting requirements if those spells aren\'t kicked, and you can\'t kick those spells unless you can choose the appropriate targets. On the other hand, you can kick a permanent spell even if you won\'t be able to choose targets for an enters-the-battlefield ability of that permanent once the spell resolves."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "To determine a spell\'s total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card\'s effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "You can\'t pay a kicker cost more than once."}]', "[{'date': '2009-10-01', 'text': 'A “creature spell” is any spell with the type creature, even if it has other types such as artifact or enchantment. Older cards of type summon are also creature spells.'}]", "[{'date': '2009-10-01', 'text': 'The landfall ability triggers whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control for any reason. It triggers whenever you play a land, as well as whenever a spell or ability (such as Rampant Growth) causes you to put a land onto the battlefield under your control. It will even trigger when a spell or ability causes another player to put a land onto the battlefield under your control (as can happen with Yavimaya Dryad’s ability, for example).'}, {'date': '2009-10-01', 'text': 'When a land enters the battlefield under your control, each landfall ability of the permanents you control will trigger. You can put them on the stack in any order. The last ability you put on the stack will be the first one that resolves.'}, {'date': '2017-11-17', 'text': 'Lotus Cobra’s ability isn’t a mana ability. Opponents may respond to it before you have that mana.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability doesn’t trigger if a permanent already on the battlefield becomes a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability triggers whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control for any reason. It triggers whenever you play a land, as well as whenever a spell or ability puts a land onto the battlefield under your control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Lotus Cobra’s ability uses the stack and players may respond to it. It isn’t a mana ability because the event that causes it to trigger isn’t a mana ability.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, each landfall ability of the permanents you control will trigger. You can put them on the stack in any order. The last ability you put on the stack will be the first one to resolve.'}]", "[{'date': '2018-07-13', 'text': 'You must discard exactly one card to cast Tormenting Voice; you can’t cast it without discarding a card, and you can’t discard additional cards.'}]", "[{'date': '2019-07-12', 'text': 'If either creature is an illegal target as Rabid Bite tries to resolve, the creature you control won’t deal damage.'}]", '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "A landfall ability doesn\'t trigger if a permanent already on the battlefield becomes a land."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'A landfall ability triggers whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control for any reason. It triggers whenever you play a land, as well as whenever a spell or ability puts a land onto the battlefield under your control.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "After you cast Skyclave Shade from your graveyard, it\'s considered a new object, and the permission from its landfall ability won\'t apply to it again even if it returns to your graveyard later in the turn. You\'ll need to have another land enter the battlefield under your control after it has returned to your graveyard to cast it again."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'An ability that triggers when a player casts a kicked spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell. It resolves even if that spell is countered.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If you copy a kicked spell, the copy is also kicked. If a card or token enters the battlefield as a copy of a permanent that\'s already on the battlefield, the new permanent isn\'t kicked, even if the original was."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can\'t kick it."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'Kicker represents an optional additional cost that you may choose to pay as you cast the spell. A spell cast with that additional cost paid is “kicked.”\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Skyclave Shade\'s landfall ability triggers only if it\'s in your graveyard immediately after the land enters the battlefield."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Some instant or sorcery spells require alternative or additional targets if they\'re kicked. You ignore these targeting requirements if those spells aren\'t kicked, and you can\'t kick those spells unless you can choose the appropriate targets. On the other hand, you can kick a permanent spell even if you won\'t be able to choose targets for an enters-the-battlefield ability of that permanent once the spell resolves."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "To determine a spell\'s total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card\'s effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, each landfall ability of the permanents you control will trigger. You can put them on the stack in any order. The last ability you put on the stack will be the first one to resolve.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "You can\'t pay a kicker cost more than once."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'You must follow the normal timing permissions and restrictions for Skyclave Shade when casting it with the permission of its landfall ability. You must pay its mana cost (or, if another effect allows, an alternative cost). You may pay its kicker cost when casting it this way.\'}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "A landfall ability doesn\'t trigger if a permanent already on the battlefield becomes a land."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'A landfall ability triggers whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control for any reason. It triggers whenever you play a land, as well as whenever a spell or ability puts a land onto the battlefield under your control.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Felidar Retreat\'s second mode affects only creatures you control at the time the ability resolves, including creatures you control but that for some reason didn\'t get a +1/+1 counter. Creatures you begin to control later in the turn won\'t gain vigilance or get a +1/+1 counter."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, each landfall ability of the permanents you control will trigger. You can put them on the stack in any order. The last ability you put on the stack will be the first one to resolve.\'}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "A landfall ability doesn\'t trigger if a permanent already on the battlefield becomes a land."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'A landfall ability triggers whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control for any reason. It triggers whenever you play a land, as well as whenever a spell or ability puts a land onto the battlefield under your control.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If Scute Swarm leaves the battlefield before its triggered ability resolves, the token will still enter the battlefield as a copy of Scute Swarm, using Scute Swarm\'s copiable values from when it was last on the battlefield."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "The token copy will have Scute Swarm\'s ability. It will also be able to create copies of itself."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "The token copy won\'t copy counters or damage marked on Scute Swarm, nor will it copy other effects that have changed Scute Swarm\'s power, toughness, types, color, and so on. Normally, this means the token will simply be a Scute Swarm, but if any copy effects have affected the original Scute Swarm, the token will take those into account."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, each landfall ability of the permanents you control will trigger. You can put them on the stack in any order. The last ability you put on the stack will be the first one to resolve.\'}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Activated abilities contain a colon. They\'re generally written “[Cost]: [Effect].” Some keyword abilities (such as equip) are activated abilities and will have a colon in their reminder text."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Any choices made when the spell or ability resolves won\'t have been made yet when it\'s copied. Any such choices will be made separately when the copy resolves. Most notably, if a triggered ability asks you to pay a cost (such as that of Leyline Tyrant), you pay that cost for the copy if you wish to have it paid."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If a permanent spell is copied, it\'s put onto the battlefield as a token as the spell resolves rather than putting the copy of the spell onto the battlefield. The rules that apply to a permanent spell becoming a permanent apply to a copy of a spell becoming a token."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If an ability is linked to a second ability, copies of that first ability are also linked to that second ability. If the second ability refers to “the exiled card,” it refers to all cards exiled by the first ability and the copy. For example, if Fiend Hunter\'s enters-the-battlefield ability is copied and two creatures are exiled, they both return when Fiend Hunter leaves the battlefield."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If the spell or ability has damage divided as it was put onto the stack, the division can\'t be changed, although the targets receiving that damage still can. The same is true of spells and abilities that distribute counters."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If the spell or ability that\'s copied has an X whose value was determined as it was cast or activated, the copy will have the same value of X."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If the spell or ability that\'s copied is modal (that is, it says “Choose one —” or the like), the copy will have the same mode. A different mode can\'t be chosen. This doesn\'t apply to copying a permanent spell with a modal enters-the-battlefield triggered ability, but it does apply to copying that ability."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Lithoform Engine can copy any spell or ability on the stack, not just one with targets. If a permanent spell is copied, new targets can\'t be chosen for it, if it has any (perhaps because it\'s an Aura or a mutating creature spell)."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Lithoform Engine\'s first ability targets an activated or triggered ability that is on the stack and creates another instance of that ability on the stack. It doesn\'t cause any object to gain an ability."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "The copy is created on the stack, so it\'s not “cast” or “activated.” Creating the copy won\'t cause abilities that trigger when a player casts a spell or activates an ability to trigger. Abilities that say that a triggered ability triggers additional times won\'t apply to copying a triggered ability."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "The copy will have the same targets as the spell or ability it\'s copying unless you choose new ones. You may change any number of the targets, including all of them or none of them. If, for one of the targets, you can\'t choose a new legal target, then it remains unchanged (even if the current target is illegal)."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'The copy will resolve before the original spell or ability does.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "The source of the copy from Lithoform Engine\'s first ability is the same as the source of the original ability."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "The token that a resolving copy of a spell becomes isn\'t said to have been “created.”"}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Triggered abilities use the word “when,” “whenever,” or “at.” They\'re often written as “[Trigger condition], [effect].” Some keywords (such as prowess) are triggered abilities and will use “when,” “whenever,” or “at” in their reminder text."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "You can\'t choose to pay any alternative or additional costs for the copy. However, effects based on any alternative or additional costs that were paid for the original spell are copied as though those same costs were paid for the copy. Most notably, if the original spell was kicked, the copy is kicked."}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can\'t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Archpriest of Iona\'s power is constantly updated as the number of creatures in your party changes. If Archpriest of Iona is on the battlefield, it will consider itself as a Cleric."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can\'t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'Once the target creature gets +1/+1 and gains flying, it keeps those bonuses even if you no longer have a full party later in the turn.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'Some cards refer to you having a “full party.” This is true if the number of creatures in your party is four.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "The ability that defines Archpriest of Iona\'s power applies in all zones, not just the battlefield."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "The last ability won\'t trigger at all if you don\'t have a full party as your combat phase begins. It won\'t grant +1/+1 or flying if you don\'t have a full party as it resolves. The number of creatures in your party may change between these times, however."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.\'}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can\'t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can\'t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If an ability of a creature counts the number of creatures in your party, that number is counted as the ability resolves. If that creature is still on the battlefield when the ability resolves, it\'ll be counted if appropriate."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If there are no creatures in your party as Acquisitions Expert\'s ability resolves, the target opponent reveals no cards and you choose no card."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'To determine "the number of creatures in your party," check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.\'}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can\'t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can\'t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If an ability of a creature counts the number of creatures in your party, that number is counted as the ability resolves. If that creature is still on the battlefield when the ability resolves, it\'ll be counted if appropriate."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If there are no creatures in your party as Cascade Seer\'s ability resolves, you don\'t scry at all. Abilities that trigger whenever you scry don\'t trigger."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.\'}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can\'t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can\'t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If an ability of a creature counts the number of creatures in your party, that number is counted as the ability resolves. If that creature is still on the battlefield when the ability resolves, it\'ll be counted if appropriate."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "In a Two-Headed Giant game, Malakir Blood-Priest\'s ability causes the opposing team to lose twice X life and you to gain X life."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.\'}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can\'t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can\'t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If an ability of a creature counts the number of creatures in your party, that number is counted as the ability resolves. If that creature is still on the battlefield when the ability resolves, it\'ll be counted if appropriate."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Once Squad Commander\'s last ability has resolved, the affected creatures won\'t lose +1/+0 or indestructible if you no longer have a full party."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'Some cards refer to you having a “full party.” This is true if the number of creatures in your party is four.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Squad Commander\'s last ability affects only creatures you control at the time it resolves. Creatures you begin to control later in the turn won\'t get +1/+0 or gain indestructible."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.\'}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can\'t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can\'t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'If a spell has a cost reduction based on the number of creatures in your party, no player may attempt to change that number after you begin to cast the spell but before you pay the cost.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Several cards have a cost reduction based on the number of creatures in your party. To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost you\'re paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Thwart the Grave\'s first target doesn\'t have to be one of the party creature types."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.\'}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "An ability that triggers whenever you play a land won\'t trigger an additional time."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Ancient Greenwarden allows you to play a modal double-faced card\'s land face, but not a nonland face."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Ancient Greenwarden doesn\'t allow you to activate abilities (such as cycling) of land cards in your graveyard."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Ancient Greenwarden doesn\'t change the times when you can play those lands. You can still play only one land per turn, and only during your main phase when you have priority and the stack is empty."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Ancient Greenwarden\'s effect doesn\'t copy the triggered ability; it causes the ability to trigger twice. Any choices made as you put the ability onto the stack, such as modes and targets, are made separately for each instance of the ability. Any choices made on resolution, such as whether to put counters on a permanent, are also made individually."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'Ancient Greenwarden\\\'s third ability affects a land\\\'s own enters-the-battlefield triggered abilities as well as other triggered abilities that trigger when that land enters the battlefield, such as landfall abilities. Such triggered abilities start with "when" or "whenever."\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'If a land entering the battlefield at the same time as Ancient Greenwarden (including Ancient Greenwarden itself if an effect causes it to be a land) causes a triggered ability of a permanent you control to trigger, that ability triggers an additional time.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'If you control two Ancient Greenwardens, a land entering the battlefield causes abilities to trigger three times, not four. A third Ancient Greenwarden causes abilities to trigger four times, a fourth causes abilities to trigger five times, and so on.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'Look at each permanent as it exists on the battlefield, taking into account continuous effects, to determine whether any triggered abilities will trigger multiple times. For example, if you control Ashaya, Soul of the Wild, a nontoken creature entering the battlefield will cause any appropriate abilities to trigger an additional time.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'Replacement effects are unaffected by Ancient Greenwarden\\\'s third ability. This includes any abilities that apply "as [this land] enters the battlefield" and any ability that says the land enters the battlefield with counters.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'The trigger event doesn\\\'t have to specifically refer to "lands." For example, an ability that triggers "whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control" would trigger twice if the entering land is also a creature.\'}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Attaching an Equipment with its enters-the-battlefield triggered ability isn\'t the same as using its equip ability. You don\'t pay mana for the attachment, and if the Equipment enters at a time you couldn\'t cast a sorcery, you can still attach it to a creature you control."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'If the target creature becomes an illegal target, the Equipment remains on the battlefield unattached.\'}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If the target creature is an illegal target by the time Pressure Point tries to resolve, the spell doesn\'t resolve. You don\'t draw a card. If the target is legal but doesn\'t become tapped (most likely because it\'s already tapped), you do draw a card."}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Kaza\'s cost reduction can reduce only generic mana in a spell\'s cost. It can\'t reduce colored mana requirements."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost you\'re paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions (such as that of Kaza\'s activated ability). The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was."}]', "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A Wizard spell is one with the creature type Wizard. Spells that are Wizard-themed (such as Relic Amulet) aren’t Wizard spells.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A modal double-faced card can’t be transformed or be put onto the battlefield transformed. Ignore any instruction to transform a modal double-faced card or to put one onto the battlefield transformed.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell (if it has any targets). The ability resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a land or cast a spell from among a group of cards, you may play or cast a modal double-faced card with any face that fits the criteria of that effect.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a specific modal double-faced card, you may cast it as a spell or play it as a land, as determined by which face you choose to play. If an effect allows you to cast (rather than “play”) a specific modal double-faced card, you can’t play it as a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect instructs a player to choose a card name, the name of either face may be chosen. If that effect or a linked ability refers to a spell with the chosen name being cast and/or a land with the chosen name being played, it considers only the chosen name, not the other face’s name.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect puts a double-faced card onto the battlefield, it enters with its front face up. If that front face can’t be put onto the battlefield, it doesn’t enter the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In the Commander variant, a double-faced card’s color identity is determined by the mana costs and mana symbols in the rules text of both faces combined. If either face has a color indicator or basic land type, those are also considered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The converted mana cost of a modal double-faced card is based on the characteristics of the face that’s being considered. On the stack and battlefield, consider whichever face is up. In all other zones, consider only the front face. This is different than how the converted mana cost of a transforming double-faced card is determined.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'There is a single triangle icon in the top left corner of the front face. There is a double triangle icon in the top left corner of the back face.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine whether it is legal to play a modal double-faced card, consider only the characteristics of the face you’re playing and ignore the other face’s characteristics.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A Wizard spell is one with the creature type Wizard. Spells that are Wizard-themed (such as Relic Amulet) aren’t Wizard spells.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell (if it has any targets). The ability resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Because damage remains marked on a creature until the damage is removed as the turn ends, nonlethal damage dealt to Master of Winds may become lethal if you change its base toughness during that turn.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Effects that modify the power or toughness of Master of Winds without setting it will apply to its new base power and toughness no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for counters that change its power and toughness.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The ability of Master of Winds overwrites any previous effects that set its power and/or toughness to specific values. Other effects that set these characteristics to specific values that start to apply after the ability resolves will overwrite that part of the effect.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You don’t choose a power and toughness for Master of Winds as its ability triggers. Rather, as it resolves, you choose whether to have Master of Winds become 4/1, become 1/4, or not change its power and toughness.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A Wizard spell is one with the creature type Wizard. Spells that are Wizard-themed (such as Relic Amulet) aren’t Wizard spells.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell (if it has any targets). The ability resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You draw a card and discard a card while Windrider Wizard’s last ability is resolving. No player may take actions between those events, and nothing can happen.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A Wizard spell is one with the creature type Wizard. Spells that are Wizard-themed (such as Relic Amulet) aren’t Wizard spells.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell (if it has any targets). The ability resolves even if that spell is countered.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A copy is created even if Sea Gate Stormcaller leaves the battlefield before its delayed triggered ability is created.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A copy is created even if the spell that caused Sea Gate Stormcaller’s delayed triggered ability to trigger has been countered by the time that ability resolves. The copy resolves before the original spell.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a kicked spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell. It resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'For spells with {X} in their mana costs, use the value chosen for X to determine the spell’s converted mana cost. If it’s copied, the copy has the same value of X.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the spell that’s copied is modal (that is, it says “Choose one —” or the like), the copy will have the same mode or modes. You can’t choose different ones.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you copy a kicked spell, the copy is also kicked. If a card or token enters the battlefield as a copy of a permanent that’s already on the battlefield, the new permanent isn’t kicked, even if the original was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can’t kick it.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Kicker represents an optional additional cost that you may choose to pay as you cast the spell. A spell cast with that additional cost paid is “kicked.”'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Sea Gate Stormcaller’s delayed triggered ability will copy any instant or sorcery spell, not just one with targets.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Some instant or sorcery spells require alternative or additional targets if they’re kicked. You ignore these targeting requirements if those spells aren’t kicked, and you can’t kick those spells unless you can choose the appropriate targets. On the other hand, you can kick a permanent spell even if you won’t be able to choose targets for an enters-the-battlefield ability of that permanent once the spell resolves.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The copy is created on the stack, so it’s not “cast.” Abilities that trigger when a player casts a spell won’t trigger.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The copy will have the same targets as the spell it’s copying unless you choose new ones. You may change any number of the targets, including all of them or none of them. The new targets must be legal.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine a spell’s total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card’s effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The converted mana cost of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can’t choose to pay any additional costs for the copy. However, effects based on any additional costs that were paid for the original spell are copied as though those same costs were paid for the copy too. Notably, if the spell you copy was kicked, the copy or copies will also be kicked.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can’t pay a kicker cost more than once.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A copy is created even if the spell that caused Verazol’s last ability to trigger has been countered by the time that ability resolves. The copy resolves before the original spell.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'For spells with {X} in their mana costs, the copy has the same value of X.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If Verazol enters the battlefield without being cast, then no mana was spent to cast it. It enters the battlefield without any +1/+1 counters. If no other effects are increasing its toughness at that time, it will be put into its owner’s graveyard as a state-based action.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a permanent spell is copied, it’s put onto the battlefield as a token as the spell resolves rather than putting the copy of the spell onto the battlefield. The rules that apply to a permanent spell becoming a permanent apply to a copy of a spell becoming a token.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If another creature enters the battlefield as a copy of Verazol, consider how much mana was spent to cast that creature to determine how many +1/+1 counters it enters with.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the spell that’s copied is modal (that is, it says “Choose one —” or the like), the copy will have the same mode or modes. You can’t choose different ones. This doesn’t apply to copying a permanent spell with a modal enters-the-battlefield ability.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The amount of mana you spent to cast Verazol is usually equal to its converted mana cost, normally 2 plus the value chosen for X. However, you also include any additional costs you pay, including the “commander tax” in a Commander game.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The copy is created on the stack, so it’s not “cast.” Abilities that trigger when a player casts a spell won’t trigger.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The copy will have the same targets as the spell it’s copying unless you choose new ones. You may change any number of the targets, including all of them or none of them. The new targets must be legal.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The token that a resolving copy of a spell becomes isn’t said to have been “created.”'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Verazol’s last ability can copy any kicked spell, not just one with targets.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can’t choose to pay any additional costs for the copy. However, effects based on any additional costs that were paid for the original spell are copied as though those same costs were paid for the copy too. Most notably, the copy is also kicked.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can’t remove more than two counters as Verazol’s last ability resolves to copy the spell more than once. You can’t remove just one counter from it if it has only one. If Verazol leaves the battlefield while its last ability is on the stack, you can’t remove two +1/+1 counters from it at all.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A creature that enters the battlefield attacking hasn’t attacked that combat. Moraug’s ability won’t count that combat. Unless that creature has haste, it won’t be able to attack in additional combats this turn.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability doesn’t trigger if a permanent already on the battlefield becomes a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability triggers whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control for any reason. It triggers whenever you play a land, as well as whenever a spell or ability puts a land onto the battlefield under your control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the landfall ability resolves during your precombat main phase, the additional combat phase will happen before your regular combat phase. You’ll untap creatures you control at the beginning of the additional combat but not at the beginning of your regular combat.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Moraug’s first ability checks each turn how many times each creature has attacked. It counts times that creature attacked before Moraug was on the battlefield, and it stops applying if Moraug leaves the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Moraug’s first ability counts how many times a creature has attacked, not how many times it has dealt damage. The first time a creature attacks in a turn, the +1/+0 bonus will apply to the combat damage it deals during that combat.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'There won’t be an additional main phase after the additional combat phase. For example, if the landfall ability resolves twice during your postcombat main phase, you’ll get two consecutive additional combat phases after your main phase (untapping your creatures at the beginning of each), followed by your ending phase.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, each landfall ability of the permanents you control will trigger. You can put them on the stack in any order. The last ability you put on the stack will be the first one to resolve.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A land is normally colorless, regardless of what colors of mana that land can produce. If an effect makes a colorless land into a creature without specifying that it becomes a certain color, the land creature gets +2/+2.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger. It resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Forsaken Monument’s last ability won’t trigger when you play a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you tap a permanent for more than one {C}, you add only one additional {C}.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You “tap a permanent for {C}” only if you activate a mana ability of that permanent that includes the {T} symbol in its cost, and only if it produces one or more {C} as it resolves.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A land that’s a Forest has the intrinsic mana ability “{T}: Add {G}.”'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'As long as Ashaya is on the battlefield, it’s affected by its second ability and thus its first ability counts itself.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Because damage remains marked on a creature until the damage is removed as the turn ends, nonlethal damage dealt to Ashaya may become lethal if lands you control leave the battlefield during that turn.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The ability that defines Ashaya’s power and toughness applies in all zones, not just the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can’t play creature cards as lands; you’ll still have to cast them as spells, and they’ll enter the battlefield as lands (in addition to their other types).'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability doesn’t trigger if a permanent already on the battlefield becomes a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability triggers whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control for any reason. It triggers whenever you play a land, as well as whenever a spell or ability puts a land onto the battlefield under your control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A modal double-faced card can’t be transformed or be put onto the battlefield transformed. Ignore any instruction to transform a modal double-faced card or to put one onto the battlefield transformed.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a land or cast a spell from among a group of cards, you may play or cast a modal double-faced card with any face that fits the criteria of that effect.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a specific modal double-faced card, you may cast it as a spell or play it as a land, as determined by which face you choose to play. If an effect allows you to cast (rather than “play”) a specific modal double-faced card, you can’t play it as a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect instructs a player to choose a card name, the name of either face may be chosen. If that effect or a linked ability refers to a spell with the chosen name being cast and/or a land with the chosen name being played, it considers only the chosen name, not the other face’s name.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect puts a double-faced card onto the battlefield, it enters with its front face up. If that front face can’t be put onto the battlefield, it doesn’t enter the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In the Commander variant, a double-faced card’s color identity is determined by the mana costs and mana symbols in the rules text of both faces combined. If either face has a color indicator or basic land type, those are also considered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The converted mana cost of a modal double-faced card is based on the characteristics of the face that’s being considered. On the stack and battlefield, consider whichever face is up. In all other zones, consider only the front face. This is different than how the converted mana cost of a transforming double-faced card is determined.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'There is a single triangle icon in the top left corner of the front face. There is a double triangle icon in the top left corner of the back face.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine whether it is legal to play a modal double-faced card, consider only the characteristics of the face you’re playing and ignore the other face’s characteristics.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, each landfall ability of the permanents you control will trigger. You can put them on the stack in any order. The last ability you put on the stack will be the first one to resolve.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability doesn’t trigger if a permanent already on the battlefield becomes a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability triggers whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control for any reason. It triggers whenever you play a land, as well as whenever a spell or ability puts a land onto the battlefield under your control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Attaching an Equipment with its enters-the-battlefield triggered ability isn’t the same as using its equip ability. You don’t pay mana for the attachment, and if the Equipment enters at a time you couldn’t cast a sorcery, you can still attach it to a creature you control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the target creature becomes an illegal target, the Equipment remains on the battlefield unattached.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If there’s no equipped creature as Skyclave Pick-Axe’s landfall ability resolves, no creature gets +2/+2.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The bonus from Skyclave Pick-Axe’s landfall ability applies to the creature it’s attached to at the time the ability resolves. That bonus doesn’t apply to a new creature if Skyclave Pick-Axe becomes attached to a new creature.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, each landfall ability of the permanents you control will trigger. You can put them on the stack in any order. The last ability you put on the stack will be the first one to resolve.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability doesn’t trigger if a permanent already on the battlefield becomes a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability triggers whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control for any reason. It triggers whenever you play a land, as well as whenever a spell or ability puts a land onto the battlefield under your control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Canyon Jerboa’s ability affects only creatures you control at the time it resolves. Creatures you begin to control later in the turn won’t get +1/+1.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, each landfall ability of the permanents you control will trigger. You can put them on the stack in any order. The last ability you put on the stack will be the first one to resolve.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability doesn’t trigger if a permanent already on the battlefield becomes a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability triggers whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control for any reason. It triggers whenever you play a land, as well as whenever a spell or ability puts a land onto the battlefield under your control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Effects that modify the power or toughness of the land creature without setting it will apply to its new base power and toughness no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for counters that change its power and toughness.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a card in a player’s hand or graveyard has {X} in its mana cost, X is considered to be 0.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Nissa’s middle ability can target a land that’s already untapped or that’s already a creature.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Nissa’s middle ability doesn’t remove any abilities the land creature has.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Nissa’s middle ability overwrites any previous effects that set the land creature’s power and/or toughness to specific values. Other effects that set these characteristics to specific values that start to apply after the ability resolves will overwrite that part of the effect.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The creature card’s converted mana cost is checked only in your hand or graveyard. You may put a creature card onto the battlefield whose converted mana cost becomes greater than the number of lands you control once it’s on the battlefield, most likely because it enters as a copy of another permanent.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, each landfall ability of the permanents you control will trigger. You can put them on the stack in any order. The last ability you put on the stack will be the first one to resolve.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability doesn’t trigger if a permanent already on the battlefield becomes a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability triggers whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control for any reason. It triggers whenever you play a land, as well as whenever a spell or ability puts a land onto the battlefield under your control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If Valakut Exploration leaves the battlefield, any cards exiled with it remain exiled and can be played. The end step triggered ability won’t trigger, and the cards won’t be put into their owner’s graveyard.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you play a card this way, it leaves exile and becomes a new object. If it returns to exile later in the turn, you can’t play it again.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you play the card in response to the end step triggered ability, that card won’t be put into your graveyard and won’t be counted when determining how much damage to deal.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a Two-Headed Giant game, the end step triggered ability causes the opposing team to lose 2 life for each card put into its owner’s graveyard.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, each landfall ability of the permanents you control will trigger. You can put them on the stack in any order. The last ability you put on the stack will be the first one to resolve.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You must follow the normal timing permissions and restrictions for the exiled card. If it’s a land, you can’t play it unless you have land plays available.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You’ll still pay all costs for a spell cast this way, including additional costs. You may also pay alternative costs if any are available.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability doesn’t trigger if a permanent already on the battlefield becomes a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability triggers whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control for any reason. It triggers whenever you play a land, as well as whenever a spell or ability puts a land onto the battlefield under your control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a Two-Headed Giant game, Omnath’s second ability causes the opposing team to lose 8 life the third time it resolves. Each other player’s planeswalkers—including your teammate’s—are dealt 4 damage.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Omnath’s landfall ability always uses the stack and players may respond to it. It isn’t a mana ability because the event that causes it to trigger isn’t a mana ability, even if it’s the second time the ability has resolved in a turn.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Omnath’s landfall ability has no effect each time beyond the third it resolves in a turn.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, each landfall ability of the permanents you control will trigger. You can put them on the stack in any order. The last ability you put on the stack will be the first one to resolve.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability doesn’t trigger if a permanent already on the battlefield becomes a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability triggers whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control for any reason. It triggers whenever you play a land, as well as whenever a spell or ability puts a land onto the battlefield under your control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a Two-Headed Giant game, Spitfire Lagac’s ability causes the opposing team to lose 2 life.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, each landfall ability of the permanents you control will trigger. You can put them on the stack in any order. The last ability you put on the stack will be the first one to resolve.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability doesn’t trigger if a permanent already on the battlefield becomes a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability triggers whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control for any reason. It triggers whenever you play a land, as well as whenever a spell or ability puts a land onto the battlefield under your control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Once a creature with power 3 or greater has blocked this creature, changing the power of the blocking creature won’t cause this creature to become unblocked.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, each landfall ability of the permanents you control will trigger. You can put them on the stack in any order. The last ability you put on the stack will be the first one to resolve.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability doesn’t trigger if a permanent already on the battlefield becomes a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A landfall ability triggers whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control for any reason. It triggers whenever you play a land, as well as whenever a spell or ability puts a land onto the battlefield under your control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, each landfall ability of the permanents you control will trigger. You can put them on the stack in any order. The last ability you put on the stack will be the first one to resolve.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A modal double-faced card can’t be transformed or be put onto the battlefield transformed. Ignore any instruction to transform a modal double-faced card or to put one onto the battlefield transformed.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that offers a bonus if an opponent has eight or more cards in their graveyard won’t provide additional benefits if more than one opponent has eight or more cards in their graveyard. There are also no additional benefits no matter how many cards are in an opponent’s graveyard, as long as there are at least eight.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a land or cast a spell from among a group of cards, you may play or cast a modal double-faced card with any face that fits the criteria of that effect.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a specific modal double-faced card, you may cast it as a spell or play it as a land, as determined by which face you choose to play. If an effect allows you to cast (rather than “play”) a specific modal double-faced card, you can’t play it as a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect instructs a player to choose a card name, the name of either face may be chosen. If that effect or a linked ability refers to a spell with the chosen name being cast and/or a land with the chosen name being played, it considers only the chosen name, not the other face’s name.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect puts a double-faced card onto the battlefield, it enters with its front face up. If that front face can’t be put onto the battlefield, it doesn’t enter the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a multiplayer game, once an opponent leaves the game, they won’t be considered for such an effect, no matter how many cards they had in their graveyard before leaving the game.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In the Commander variant, a double-faced card’s color identity is determined by the mana costs and mana symbols in the rules text of both faces combined. If either face has a color indicator or basic land type, those are also considered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The mana value of a modal double-faced card is based on the characteristics of the face that’s being considered. On the stack and battlefield, consider whichever face is up. In all other zones, consider only the front face. This is different than how the mana value of a transforming double-faced card is determined.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'There is a single triangle icon in the top left corner of the front face. There is a double triangle icon in the top left corner of the back face.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine whether it is legal to play a modal double-faced card, consider only the characteristics of the face you’re playing and ignore the other face’s characteristics.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A modal double-faced card can’t be transformed or be put onto the battlefield transformed. Ignore any instruction to transform a modal double-faced card or to put one onto the battlefield transformed.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Any enters-the-battlefield abilities of the copied creature will trigger when Glasspool Mimic enters the battlefield. Any “as [this creature] enters the battlefield” or “[this creature] enters the battlefield with” abilities of the chosen creature will also work.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Glasspool Mimic copies exactly what was printed on the original creature (unless that creature is copying something else or is a token; see below), except that it’s also a Shapeshifter Rogue. It doesn’t copy whether that creature is tapped or untapped, whether it has any counters on it or any Auras and Equipment attached to it, or any non-copy effects that have changed its power, toughness, types, color, or so on. Most notably, if it copies a creature that’s not normally a creature, it won’t be a creature.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If Glasspool Mimic isn’t a creature, most likely because it copied a creature that was only temporarily a creature, it won’t be a Shapeshifter Rogue, even if it becomes a creature later.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If Glasspool Mimic somehow enters the battlefield at the same time as another creature, it can’t become a copy of that creature. You may choose only a creature that’s already on the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a land or cast a spell from among a group of cards, you may play or cast a modal double-faced card with any face that fits the criteria of that effect.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a specific modal double-faced card, you may cast it as a spell or play it as a land, as determined by which face you choose to play. If an effect allows you to cast (rather than “play”) a specific modal double-faced card, you can’t play it as a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect instructs a player to choose a card name, the name of either face may be chosen. If that effect or a linked ability refers to a spell with the chosen name being cast and/or a land with the chosen name being played, it considers only the chosen name, not the other face’s name.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect puts a double-faced card onto the battlefield, it enters with its front face up. If that front face can’t be put onto the battlefield, it doesn’t enter the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If another creature becomes a copy of Glasspool Mimic, that creature is also a Shapeshifter Rogue.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the chosen creature is a token, Glasspool Mimic copies the original characteristics of that token as stated by the effect that put the token onto the battlefield. Glasspool Mimic doesn’t become a token in this case.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the chosen creature is copying something else (for example, if the chosen creature is another Glasspool Mimic), then Glasspool Mimic enters the battlefield as whatever the chosen creature copied.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the copied creature has {X} in its mana cost, X is considered to be 0.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In the Commander variant, a double-faced card’s color identity is determined by the mana costs and mana symbols in the rules text of both faces combined. If either face has a color indicator or basic land type, those are also considered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The converted mana cost of a modal double-faced card is based on the characteristics of the face that’s being considered. On the stack and battlefield, consider whichever face is up. In all other zones, consider only the front face. This is different than how the converted mana cost of a transforming double-faced card is determined.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'There is a single triangle icon in the top left corner of the front face. There is a double triangle icon in the top left corner of the back face.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine whether it is legal to play a modal double-faced card, consider only the characteristics of the face you’re playing and ignore the other face’s characteristics.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A modal double-faced card can’t be transformed or be put onto the battlefield transformed. Ignore any instruction to transform a modal double-faced card or to put one onto the battlefield transformed.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Gaining control of a creature doesn’t cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a land or cast a spell from among a group of cards, you may play or cast a modal double-faced card with any face that fits the criteria of that effect.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a specific modal double-faced card, you may cast it as a spell or play it as a land, as determined by which face you choose to play. If an effect allows you to cast (rather than “play”) a specific modal double-faced card, you can’t play it as a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect instructs a player to choose a card name, the name of either face may be chosen. If that effect or a linked ability refers to a spell with the chosen name being cast and/or a land with the chosen name being played, it considers only the chosen name, not the other face’s name.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect puts a double-faced card onto the battlefield, it enters with its front face up. If that front face can’t be put onto the battlefield, it doesn’t enter the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In the Commander variant, a double-faced card’s color identity is determined by the mana costs and mana symbols in the rules text of both faces combined. If either face has a color indicator or basic land type, those are also considered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Song-Mad Treachery can target any creature, even one that’s untapped or one you already control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The converted mana cost of a modal double-faced card is based on the characteristics of the face that’s being considered. On the stack and battlefield, consider whichever face is up. In all other zones, consider only the front face. This is different than how the converted mana cost of a transforming double-faced card is determined.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'There is a single triangle icon in the top left corner of the front face. There is a double triangle icon in the top left corner of the back face.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine whether it is legal to play a modal double-faced card, consider only the characteristics of the face you’re playing and ignore the other face’s characteristics.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A modal double-faced card can’t be transformed or be put onto the battlefield transformed. Ignore any instruction to transform a modal double-faced card or to put one onto the battlefield transformed.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Hagra Mauling’s first ability reduces the cost by only {1}, even if you have two opponents with no basic lands. It reduces the cost even if some opponents control basic lands, as long as one controls no basic lands.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a land or cast a spell from among a group of cards, you may play or cast a modal double-faced card with any face that fits the criteria of that effect.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a specific modal double-faced card, you may cast it as a spell or play it as a land, as determined by which face you choose to play. If an effect allows you to cast (rather than “play”) a specific modal double-faced card, you can’t play it as a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect instructs a player to choose a card name, the name of either face may be chosen. If that effect or a linked ability refers to a spell with the chosen name being cast and/or a land with the chosen name being played, it considers only the chosen name, not the other face’s name.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect puts a double-faced card onto the battlefield, it enters with its front face up. If that front face can’t be put onto the battlefield, it doesn’t enter the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In the Commander variant, a double-faced card’s color identity is determined by the mana costs and mana symbols in the rules text of both faces combined. If either face has a color indicator or basic land type, those are also considered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The converted mana cost of a modal double-faced card is based on the characteristics of the face that’s being considered. On the stack and battlefield, consider whichever face is up. In all other zones, consider only the front face. This is different than how the converted mana cost of a transforming double-faced card is determined.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The opponent who controls no basic lands doesn’t have to be the controller of the target creature for Hagra Mauling’s cost to be reduced.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'There is a single triangle icon in the top left corner of the front face. There is a double triangle icon in the top left corner of the back face.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine whether it is legal to play a modal double-faced card, consider only the characteristics of the face you’re playing and ignore the other face’s characteristics.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A modal double-faced card can’t be transformed or be put onto the battlefield transformed. Ignore any instruction to transform a modal double-faced card or to put one onto the battlefield transformed.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If X is 6 or more, you divide twice X damage; you don’t assign X damage and then double that damage.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a land or cast a spell from among a group of cards, you may play or cast a modal double-faced card with any face that fits the criteria of that effect.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a specific modal double-faced card, you may cast it as a spell or play it as a land, as determined by which face you choose to play. If an effect allows you to cast (rather than “play”) a specific modal double-faced card, you can’t play it as a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect instructs a player to choose a card name, the name of either face may be chosen. If that effect or a linked ability refers to a spell with the chosen name being cast and/or a land with the chosen name being played, it considers only the chosen name, not the other face’s name.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect puts a double-faced card onto the battlefield, it enters with its front face up. If that front face can’t be put onto the battlefield, it doesn’t enter the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If one of the targets becomes illegal for Shatterskull Smashing, the original division of damage still applies to the still-legal target, but the damage that would have been dealt to the illegal target isn’t dealt at all.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In the Commander variant, a double-faced card’s color identity is determined by the mana costs and mana symbols in the rules text of both faces combined. If either face has a color indicator or basic land type, those are also considered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The converted mana cost of a modal double-faced card is based on the characteristics of the face that’s being considered. On the stack and battlefield, consider whichever face is up. In all other zones, consider only the front face. This is different than how the converted mana cost of a transforming double-faced card is determined.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'There is a single triangle icon in the top left corner of the front face. There is a double triangle icon in the top left corner of the back face.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine whether it is legal to play a modal double-faced card, consider only the characteristics of the face you’re playing and ignore the other face’s characteristics.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You divide the damage as you cast Shatterskull Smashing, not as it resolves. If you choose two targets, each target must be assigned at least 1 damage.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A modal double-faced card can’t be transformed or be put onto the battlefield transformed. Ignore any instruction to transform a modal double-faced card or to put one onto the battlefield transformed.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a card in a player’s hand has {X} in its mana cost, X is considered to be 0.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a land or cast a spell from among a group of cards, you may play or cast a modal double-faced card with any face that fits the criteria of that effect.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a specific modal double-faced card, you may cast it as a spell or play it as a land, as determined by which face you choose to play. If an effect allows you to cast (rather than “play”) a specific modal double-faced card, you can’t play it as a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect instructs a player to choose a card name, the name of either face may be chosen. If that effect or a linked ability refers to a spell with the chosen name being cast and/or a land with the chosen name being played, it considers only the chosen name, not the other face’s name.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect puts a double-faced card onto the battlefield, it enters with its front face up. If that front face can’t be put onto the battlefield, it doesn’t enter the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In the Commander variant, a double-faced card’s color identity is determined by the mana costs and mana symbols in the rules text of both faces combined. If either face has a color indicator or basic land type, those are also considered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The converted mana cost of a modal double-faced card is based on the characteristics of the face that’s being considered. On the stack and battlefield, consider whichever face is up. In all other zones, consider only the front face. This is different than how the converted mana cost of a transforming double-faced card is determined.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'There is a single triangle icon in the top left corner of the front face. There is a double triangle icon in the top left corner of the back face.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine whether it is legal to play a modal double-faced card, consider only the characteristics of the face you’re playing and ignore the other face’s characteristics.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A modal double-faced card can’t be transformed or be put onto the battlefield transformed. Ignore any instruction to transform a modal double-faced card or to put one onto the battlefield transformed.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a card in a player’s library has {X} in its mana cost, X is considered to be 0.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a land or cast a spell from among a group of cards, you may play or cast a modal double-faced card with any face that fits the criteria of that effect.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a specific modal double-faced card, you may cast it as a spell or play it as a land, as determined by which face you choose to play. If an effect allows you to cast (rather than “play”) a specific modal double-faced card, you can’t play it as a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect instructs a player to choose a card name, the name of either face may be chosen. If that effect or a linked ability refers to a spell with the chosen name being cast and/or a land with the chosen name being played, it considers only the chosen name, not the other face’s name.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect puts a double-faced card onto the battlefield, it enters with its front face up. If that front face can’t be put onto the battlefield, it doesn’t enter the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In the Commander variant, a double-faced card’s color identity is determined by the mana costs and mana symbols in the rules text of both faces combined. If either face has a color indicator or basic land type, those are also considered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The converted mana cost of a modal double-faced card is based on the characteristics of the face that’s being considered. On the stack and battlefield, consider whichever face is up. In all other zones, consider only the front face. This is different than how the converted mana cost of a transforming double-faced card is determined.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'There is a single triangle icon in the top left corner of the front face. There is a double triangle icon in the top left corner of the back face.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine whether it is legal to play a modal double-faced card, consider only the characteristics of the face you’re playing and ignore the other face’s characteristics.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Use the converted mana cost of the creature card as it exists in your library to determine whether it receives +1/+1 counters, ignoring any replacement effects (such as that of Glasspool Mimic) that will change its converted mana cost once it’s on the battlefield.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A modal double-faced card can’t be transformed or be put onto the battlefield transformed. Ignore any instruction to transform a modal double-faced card or to put one onto the battlefield transformed.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a land or cast a spell from among a group of cards, you may play or cast a modal double-faced card with any face that fits the criteria of that effect.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a specific modal double-faced card, you may cast it as a spell or play it as a land, as determined by which face you choose to play. If an effect allows you to cast (rather than “play”) a specific modal double-faced card, you can’t play it as a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect instructs a player to choose a card name, the name of either face may be chosen. If that effect or a linked ability refers to a spell with the chosen name being cast and/or a land with the chosen name being played, it considers only the chosen name, not the other face’s name.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect puts a double-faced card onto the battlefield, it enters with its front face up. If that front face can’t be put onto the battlefield, it doesn’t enter the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If either target is an illegal target as Khalni Ambush resolves, no creature will deal or be dealt damage.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In the Commander variant, a double-faced card’s color identity is determined by the mana costs and mana symbols in the rules text of both faces combined. If either face has a color indicator or basic land type, those are also considered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The converted mana cost of a modal double-faced card is based on the characteristics of the face that’s being considered. On the stack and battlefield, consider whichever face is up. In all other zones, consider only the front face. This is different than how the converted mana cost of a transforming double-faced card is determined.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'There is a single triangle icon in the top left corner of the front face. There is a double triangle icon in the top left corner of the back face.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine whether it is legal to play a modal double-faced card, consider only the characteristics of the face you’re playing and ignore the other face’s characteristics.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A modal double-faced card can’t be transformed or be put onto the battlefield transformed. Ignore any instruction to transform a modal double-faced card or to put one onto the battlefield transformed.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a land or cast a spell from among a group of cards, you may play or cast a modal double-faced card with any face that fits the criteria of that effect.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a specific modal double-faced card, you may cast it as a spell or play it as a land, as determined by which face you choose to play. If an effect allows you to cast (rather than “play”) a specific modal double-faced card, you can’t play it as a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect instructs a player to choose a card name, the name of either face may be chosen. If that effect or a linked ability refers to a spell with the chosen name being cast and/or a land with the chosen name being played, it considers only the chosen name, not the other face’s name.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect puts a double-faced card onto the battlefield, it enters with its front face up. If that front face can’t be put onto the battlefield, it doesn’t enter the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the target creature is an illegal target by the time Malakir Rebirth tries to resolve, the spell doesn’t resolve. You don’t lose 2 life.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In the Commander variant, a double-faced card’s color identity is determined by the mana costs and mana symbols in the rules text of both faces combined. If either face has a color indicator or basic land type, those are also considered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Malakir Rebirth’s effect works only once. If the targeted creature dies and is then returned to the battlefield, it’s considered to be a new creature. If that new creature dies, it won’t come back.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The converted mana cost of a modal double-faced card is based on the characteristics of the face that’s being considered. On the stack and battlefield, consider whichever face is up. In all other zones, consider only the front face. This is different than how the converted mana cost of a transforming double-faced card is determined.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'There is a single triangle icon in the top left corner of the front face. There is a double triangle icon in the top left corner of the back face.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine whether it is legal to play a modal double-faced card, consider only the characteristics of the face you’re playing and ignore the other face’s characteristics.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A modal double-faced card can’t be transformed or be put onto the battlefield transformed. Ignore any instruction to transform a modal double-faced card or to put one onto the battlefield transformed.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a land or cast a spell from among a group of cards, you may play or cast a modal double-faced card with any face that fits the criteria of that effect.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a specific modal double-faced card, you may cast it as a spell or play it as a land, as determined by which face you choose to play. If an effect allows you to cast (rather than “play”) a specific modal double-faced card, you can’t play it as a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect instructs a player to choose a card name, the name of either face may be chosen. If that effect or a linked ability refers to a spell with the chosen name being cast and/or a land with the chosen name being played, it considers only the chosen name, not the other face’s name.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect puts a double-faced card onto the battlefield, it enters with its front face up. If that front face can’t be put onto the battlefield, it doesn’t enter the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you put zero cards on the bottom of your library, you draw one card.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In the Commander variant, a double-faced card’s color identity is determined by the mana costs and mana symbols in the rules text of both faces combined. If either face has a color indicator or basic land type, those are also considered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The converted mana cost of a modal double-faced card is based on the characteristics of the face that’s being considered. On the stack and battlefield, consider whichever face is up. In all other zones, consider only the front face. This is different than how the converted mana cost of a transforming double-faced card is determined.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'There is a single triangle icon in the top left corner of the front face. There is a double triangle icon in the top left corner of the back face.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine whether it is legal to play a modal double-faced card, consider only the characteristics of the face you’re playing and ignore the other face’s characteristics.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You choose how many cards to put on the bottom of your library as Valakut Awakening resolves.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A modal double-faced card can’t be transformed or be put onto the battlefield transformed. Ignore any instruction to transform a modal double-faced card or to put one onto the battlefield transformed.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a land or cast a spell from among a group of cards, you may play or cast a modal double-faced card with any face that fits the criteria of that effect.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a specific modal double-faced card, you may cast it as a spell or play it as a land, as determined by which face you choose to play. If an effect allows you to cast (rather than “play”) a specific modal double-faced card, you can’t play it as a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect instructs a player to choose a card name, the name of either face may be chosen. If that effect or a linked ability refers to a spell with the chosen name being cast and/or a land with the chosen name being played, it considers only the chosen name, not the other face’s name.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect puts a double-faced card onto the battlefield, it enters with its front face up. If that front face can’t be put onto the battlefield, it doesn’t enter the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a Two-Headed Giant game, Zof Consumption causes the opposing team to lose 8 life and you to gain 4 life.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In the Commander variant, a double-faced card’s color identity is determined by the mana costs and mana symbols in the rules text of both faces combined. If either face has a color indicator or basic land type, those are also considered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The converted mana cost of a modal double-faced card is based on the characteristics of the face that’s being considered. On the stack and battlefield, consider whichever face is up. In all other zones, consider only the front face. This is different than how the converted mana cost of a transforming double-faced card is determined.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'There is a single triangle icon in the top left corner of the front face. There is a double triangle icon in the top left corner of the back face.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine whether it is legal to play a modal double-faced card, consider only the characteristics of the face you’re playing and ignore the other face’s characteristics.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A modal double-faced card can’t be transformed or be put onto the battlefield transformed. Ignore any instruction to transform a modal double-faced card or to put one onto the battlefield transformed.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a land or cast a spell from among a group of cards, you may play or cast a modal double-faced card with any face that fits the criteria of that effect.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a specific modal double-faced card, you may cast it as a spell or play it as a land, as determined by which face you choose to play. If an effect allows you to cast (rather than “play”) a specific modal double-faced card, you can’t play it as a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect instructs a player to choose a card name, the name of either face may be chosen. If that effect or a linked ability refers to a spell with the chosen name being cast and/or a land with the chosen name being played, it considers only the chosen name, not the other face’s name.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect puts a double-faced card onto the battlefield, it enters with its front face up. If that front face can’t be put onto the battlefield, it doesn’t enter the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In the Commander variant, a double-faced card’s color identity is determined by the mana costs and mana symbols in the rules text of both faces combined. If either face has a color indicator or basic land type, those are also considered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Makindi Stampede affects only creatures you control at the time it resolves. Creatures you begin to control later in the turn won’t get +2/+2.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The converted mana cost of a modal double-faced card is based on the characteristics of the face that’s being considered. On the stack and battlefield, consider whichever face is up. In all other zones, consider only the front face. This is different than how the converted mana cost of a transforming double-faced card is determined.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'There is a single triangle icon in the top left corner of the front face. There is a double triangle icon in the top left corner of the back face.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine whether it is legal to play a modal double-faced card, consider only the characteristics of the face you’re playing and ignore the other face’s characteristics.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A modal double-faced card can’t be transformed or be put onto the battlefield transformed. Ignore any instruction to transform a modal double-faced card or to put one onto the battlefield transformed.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a land or cast a spell from among a group of cards, you may play or cast a modal double-faced card with any face that fits the criteria of that effect.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a specific modal double-faced card, you may cast it as a spell or play it as a land, as determined by which face you choose to play. If an effect allows you to cast (rather than “play”) a specific modal double-faced card, you can’t play it as a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect instructs a player to choose a card name, the name of either face may be chosen. If that effect or a linked ability refers to a spell with the chosen name being cast and/or a land with the chosen name being played, it considers only the chosen name, not the other face’s name.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect puts a double-faced card onto the battlefield, it enters with its front face up. If that front face can’t be put onto the battlefield, it doesn’t enter the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In the Commander variant, a double-faced card’s color identity is determined by the mana costs and mana symbols in the rules text of both faces combined. If either face has a color indicator or basic land type, those are also considered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The converted mana cost of a modal double-faced card is based on the characteristics of the face that’s being considered. On the stack and battlefield, consider whichever face is up. In all other zones, consider only the front face. This is different than how the converted mana cost of a transforming double-faced card is determined.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'There is a single triangle icon in the top left corner of the front face. There is a double triangle icon in the top left corner of the back face.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine whether it is legal to play a modal double-faced card, consider only the characteristics of the face you’re playing and ignore the other face’s characteristics.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A modal double-faced card can’t be transformed or be put onto the battlefield transformed. Ignore any instruction to transform a modal double-faced card or to put one onto the battlefield transformed.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a land or cast a spell from among a group of cards, you may play or cast a modal double-faced card with any face that fits the criteria of that effect.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to play a specific modal double-faced card, you may cast it as a spell or play it as a land, as determined by which face you choose to play. If an effect allows you to cast (rather than “play”) a specific modal double-faced card, you can’t play it as a land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect instructs a player to choose a card name, the name of either face may be chosen. If that effect or a linked ability refers to a spell with the chosen name being cast and/or a land with the chosen name being played, it considers only the chosen name, not the other face’s name.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect puts a double-faced card onto the battlefield, it enters with its front face up. If that front face can’t be put onto the battlefield, it doesn’t enter the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In the Commander variant, a double-faced card’s color identity is determined by the mana costs and mana symbols in the rules text of both faces combined. If either face has a color indicator or basic land type, those are also considered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The mana value of a modal double-faced card is based on the characteristics of the face that’s being considered. On the stack and battlefield, consider whichever face is up. In all other zones, consider only the front face. This is different than how the mana value of a transforming double-faced card is determined.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'There is a single triangle icon in the top left corner of the front face. There is a double triangle icon in the top left corner of the back face.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine whether it is legal to play a modal double-faced card, consider only the characteristics of the face you’re playing and ignore the other face’s characteristics.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'A spell or ability that counters spells can still target Cragplate Baloth. When that spell or ability resolves, Cragplate Baloth won’t be countered, but any additional effects of the countering spell or ability will still happen.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a kicked spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell. It resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you copy a kicked spell, the copy is also kicked. If a card or token enters the battlefield as a copy of a permanent that’s already on the battlefield, the new permanent isn’t kicked, even if the original was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can’t kick it.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Kicker represents an optional additional cost that you may choose to pay as you cast the spell. A spell cast with that additional cost paid is “kicked.”'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Some instant or sorcery spells require alternative or additional targets if they’re kicked. You ignore these targeting requirements if those spells aren’t kicked, and you can’t kick those spells unless you can choose the appropriate targets. On the other hand, you can kick a permanent spell even if you won’t be able to choose targets for an enters-the-battlefield ability of that permanent once the spell resolves.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine a spell’s total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card’s effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The converted mana cost of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can’t pay a kicker cost more than once.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Activated abilities contain a colon. They’re generally written “[Cost]: [Effect].” Some keyword abilities (such as equip) are activated abilities and will have a colon in their reminder text. Triggered abilities (starting with “when,” “whenever,” or “at”) are unaffected.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can’t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can’t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a multiplayer game, if you leave the game after Linvala’s middle ability resolves but before your next turn begins, its effect lasts until your next turn would have begun. It neither expires immediately nor lasts indefinitely.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Linvala’s middle ability won’t trigger at all if you don’t have a full party as your combat phase begins. It won’t affect the target if you don’t have a full party as it resolves. The number of creatures in your party may change between these times, however.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'No abilities of the affected permanent can be activated, including mana abilities.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Some cards refer to you having a “full party.” This is true if the number of creatures in your party is four.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The nonland permanent remains affected until your next turn even if the number of creatures in your party changes or Linvala leaves the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Activating Roiling Vortex’s last ability won’t undo any life gained before it resolved.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger. It resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a Two-Headed Giant game, Roiling Vortex’s first ability triggers twice during each team’s upkeep. Each instance deals 1 damage to one of the players on that team.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'After Nimble Trapfinder’s second ability has resolved, creatures you control keep the triggered ability for the turn even if you no longer have a full party later in the turn.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can’t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can’t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Nimble Trapfinder’s first ability checks only whether a permanent entered the battlefield under your control earlier in the turn and had one of the party creature types as it entered. It doesn’t apply if an entering object gained the type later in the turn. It does apply if the entering object left your control since. It doesn’t matter whether Nimble Trapfinder was under your control as that object entered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Nimble Trapfinder’s second ability affects only creatures you control at the time it resolves. Creatures you begin to control later in the turn won’t get the triggered ability.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Some cards refer to you having a “full party.” This is true if the number of creatures in your party is four.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Akiri’s first ability has you draw just one card per player you attack with an equipped creature, no matter how many equipped creatures you attack them with beyond the first and no matter how many Equipment that creature’s carrying beyond the first.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Equipped creatures attacking a planeswalker won’t cause Akiri’s first ability to trigger.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the creature is already tapped, it just gains indestructible until end of turn.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The Equipment that’s unattached remains on the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You choose which Equipment to unattach as Akiri’s second ability resolves. Unattaching an Equipment from a creature won’t affect other Equipment attached to that creature. No player can take actions between the time you unattach that Equipment and the time that the creature becomes tapped and gains indestructible.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'All first-strike combat damage is dealt at the same time, and, separately, all regular combat damage is dealt at the same time. If one of those amounts of combat damage is enough to cause the player being dealt damage to lose the game, Angel of Destiny’s first triggered ability has you gain life, but the other player has already lost the game and can’t gain life.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If Angel of Destiny leaves the battlefield before your end step, its last ability won’t trigger and won’t cause a player to lose the game, even if Angel of Destiny attacked that player earlier.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature you control somehow deals combat damage to you (most likely because its combat damage was redirected), you gain twice that much life as a single life-gaining event.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a Two-Headed Giant game, Angel of Destiny’s last ability can trigger as long as your team’s life total is greater than your team’s starting life total by 15 or more life.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Ally is a creature type that doesn’t appear in the Zendikar Rising set, but it has appeared in previous sets featuring the plane of Zendikar.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can’t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can’t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a spell has a cost reduction based on the number of creatures in your party, no player may attempt to change that number after you begin to cast the spell but before you pay the cost.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Several cards have a cost reduction based on the number of creatures in your party. To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost you’re paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The converted mana cost of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Tazri’s activated ability lets you put up to two cards total into your hand, not two cards of each of the listed creature types.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine the cost of Tazri’s activated ability, you choose which cost you’ll pay for each of the four mana symbols (either {2} or one mana of the appropriate color), add up the total cost, apply any additional costs, then apply any cost reductions.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Although Zareth San is attacking, it was never declared as an attacking creature (for purposes of abilities that trigger whenever a creature attacks, for example).'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Before blockers are declared, attacking Rogues are neither blocked nor unblocked, so you can’t pay the cost to activate Zareth San’s second ability.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If Zareth San leaves your hand before its second ability resolves, the ability does nothing as it resolves. Zareth San remains in its new zone and the Rogue you returned remains in its owner’s hand.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature in combat has first strike or double strike, you can activate Zareth San’s second ability during the first-strike combat damage step. Zareth San will deal combat damage during the regular combat damage step in this case, even if it somehow gains first strike.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any permanents you control from Zareth San’s last ability are exiled.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To activate Zareth San’s second ability, you reveal it in your hand. It remains revealed until the ability has resolved.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You choose which player or planeswalker Zareth San is attacking. It doesn’t have to be attacking the same player or planeswalker that the returned Rogue was attacking.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Zareth San’s second ability can be activated during the declare blockers step, combat damage step, or end of combat step. If you wait until after the declare blockers step, because all combat damage is dealt at once, Zareth San won’t normally deal combat damage.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can’t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Ardent Electromancer’s ability uses the stack and players may respond to it. It isn’t a mana ability because the event that causes it to trigger isn’t a mana ability.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can’t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an ability of a creature counts the number of creatures in your party, that number is counted as the ability resolves. If that creature is still on the battlefield when the ability resolves, it’ll be counted if appropriate.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can’t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Attaching an Equipment with its enters-the-battlefield triggered ability isn’t the same as using its equip ability. You don’t pay mana for the attachment, and if the Equipment enters at a time you couldn’t cast a sorcery, you can still attach it to a creature you control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can’t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the target creature becomes an illegal target, the Equipment remains on the battlefield unattached.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can’t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners’ graveyards. Any Equipment will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist. When the card returns to the battlefield, it will be a new object with no connection to the card that was exiled.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If Journey to Oblivion leaves the battlefield before its triggered ability resolves, the target permanent won’t be exiled.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can’t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a spell has a cost reduction based on the number of creatures in your party, no player may attempt to change that number after you begin to cast the spell but before you pay the cost.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won’t return to the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Several cards have a cost reduction based on the number of creatures in your party. To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost you’re paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The converted mana cost of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can’t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Because Emeria Captain receives its +1/+1 counters from a triggered ability rather than a replacement effect, players may take actions while that triggered ability is on the stack and Emeria Captain’s toughness is just 1.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can’t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an ability of a creature counts the number of creatures in your party, that number is counted as the ability resolves. If that creature is still on the battlefield when the ability resolves, it’ll be counted if appropriate.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can’t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can’t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a spell has a cost reduction based on the number of creatures in your party, no player may attempt to change that number after you begin to cast the spell but before you pay the cost.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the card has {X} in its mana cost, you must choose 0 as the value of X when casting it without paying its mana cost.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you cast a card “without paying its mana cost,” you can’t choose to cast it for any alternative costs. You can, however, pay additional costs. If the card has any mandatory additional costs, you must pay those to cast the card.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you have a full party and wish to cast a spell with Coveted Prize’s effect, you do so as part of the resolution of Coveted Prize after searching for a card. You can’t wait to cast it later in the turn. Timing permissions based on a card’s type are ignored.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Several cards have a cost reduction based on the number of creatures in your party. To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost you’re paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The converted mana cost of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Some cards refer to you having a “full party.” This is true if the number of creatures in your party is four.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The card you search for may be the one you cast.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can’t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can’t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a spell has a cost reduction based on the number of creatures in your party, no player may attempt to change that number after you begin to cast the spell but before you pay the cost.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Several cards have a cost reduction based on the number of creatures in your party. To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost you’re paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The converted mana cost of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The ability that adds creature types to Veteran Adventurer applies in all zones, not just the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can’t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can’t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a spell has a cost reduction based on the number of creatures in your party, no player may attempt to change that number after you begin to cast the spell but before you pay the cost.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Several cards have a cost reduction based on the number of creatures in your party. To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost you’re paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The converted mana cost of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can’t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can’t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an ability of a creature counts the number of creatures in your party, that number is counted as the ability resolves. If that creature is still on the battlefield when the ability resolves, it’ll be counted if appropriate.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The bonus is determined only as Grotag Bug-Catcher’s ability resolves. Once that happens, the size of the bonus won’t change later in the turn even if the number of creatures in your party changes.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can’t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can’t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an ability of a creature counts the number of creatures in your party, that number is counted as the ability resolves. If that creature is still on the battlefield when the ability resolves, it’ll be counted if appropriate.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The bonus is determined only as Kabira Outrider’s ability resolves. Once that happens, the size of the bonus won’t change later in the turn even if the number of creatures in your party changes.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can’t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can’t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an ability of a creature counts the number of creatures in your party, that number is counted as the ability resolves. If that creature is still on the battlefield when the ability resolves, it’ll be counted if appropriate.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can’t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can’t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the target creature is an illegal target by the time Synchronized Spellcraft tries to resolve, the spell doesn’t resolve. No player is dealt damage.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can’t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can’t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Once a creature has blocked Seafloor Stalker, activating its ability won’t cause it to become unblocked or remove that blocking creature from combat.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Once you declare that you’re activating Seafloor Stalker’s ability, no player can take actions to try and change the number of creatures in your party and change the activation cost.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can activate Seafloor Stalker’s ability more than once, even if it already can’t be blocked this turn.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can’t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can’t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The value of X is determined only as Allied Assault resolves. Once that happens, the value of X won’t change later in the turn even if the number of creatures in your party changes.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability referring to the number of creatures in your party gets a number from zero to four. Such abilities never ask which creatures are in your party, and you never have to designate specific creatures as being in your party. You can’t choose to exclude creatures from this count to lower the number.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature has more than one party creature type, and there are multiple ways to count that creature that could result in a different number of creatures in your party, the highest such number is used. For example, if you control a Cleric and a Cleric Wizard, the number of creatures in your party is two. You can’t choose to have it be just one by counting the Cleric Wizard first as a Cleric.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine “the number of creatures in your party,” check whether you control a Cleric, whether you control a Rogue, whether you control a Warrior, and whether you control a Wizard. The number is the total number of those checks to which you answered yes. Each creature you control can be counted for only one of those checks.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that offers a bonus if an opponent has eight or more cards in their graveyard won’t provide additional benefits if more than one opponent has eight or more cards in their graveyard. There are also no additional benefits no matter how many cards are in an opponent’s graveyard, as long as there are at least eight.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Anticognition can target a spell that can’t be countered. You’ll still scry 2 if an opponent has eight or more cards in their graveyard.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Anticognition will counter the spell and let you scry 2 if any opponent has eight or more cards in their graveyard, not just that spell’s controller.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an opponent has eight or more cards in their graveyard, Anticognition can still target only a creature or planeswalker spell.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a multiplayer game, once an opponent leaves the game, they won’t be considered for such an effect, no matter how many cards they had in their graveyard before leaving the game.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that offers a bonus if an opponent has eight or more cards in their graveyard won’t provide additional benefits if more than one opponent has eight or more cards in their graveyard. There are also no additional benefits no matter how many cards are in an opponent’s graveyard, as long as there are at least eight.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Attaching an Equipment with its enters-the-battlefield triggered ability isn’t the same as using its equip ability. You don’t pay mana for the attachment, and if the Equipment enters at a time you couldn’t cast a sorcery, you can still attach it to a creature you control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the target creature becomes an illegal target, the Equipment remains on the battlefield unattached.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a multiplayer game, once an opponent leaves the game, they won’t be considered for such an effect, no matter how many cards they had in their graveyard before leaving the game.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that offers a bonus if an opponent has eight or more cards in their graveyard won’t provide additional benefits if more than one opponent has eight or more cards in their graveyard. There are also no additional benefits no matter how many cards are in an opponent’s graveyard, as long as there are at least eight.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a multiplayer game, once an opponent leaves the game, they won’t be considered for such an effect, no matter how many cards they had in their graveyard before leaving the game.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Once Relic Golem has attacked, causing its first ability to apply by removing cards from graveyards won’t cause Relic Golem to be removed from combat.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Similarly, once Relic Golem has blocked an attacking creature, causing its first ability to apply won’t cause that attacking creature to become unblocked or remove Relic Golem from combat.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that offers a bonus if an opponent has eight or more cards in their graveyard won’t provide additional benefits if more than one opponent has eight or more cards in their graveyard. There are also no additional benefits no matter how many cards are in an opponent’s graveyard, as long as there are at least eight.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a multiplayer game, once an opponent leaves the game, they won’t be considered for such an effect, no matter how many cards they had in their graveyard before leaving the game.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Once a single creature has blocked Nimana Skitter-Sneak, causing it to gain menace won’t cause it to become unblocked or remove that blocking creature from combat.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that offers a bonus if an opponent has eight or more cards in their graveyard won’t provide additional benefits if more than one opponent has eight or more cards in their graveyard. There are also no additional benefits no matter how many cards are in an opponent’s graveyard, as long as there are at least eight.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a multiplayer game, once an opponent leaves the game, they won’t be considered for such an effect, no matter how many cards they had in their graveyard before leaving the game.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Soaring Thought-Thief’s fourth ability causes each opponent to mill two cards, not just those being attacked by Rogues you control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Soaring Thought-Thief’s third ability applies to itself as well as other Rogues you control.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that offers a bonus if an opponent has eight or more cards in their graveyard won’t provide additional benefits if more than one opponent has eight or more cards in their graveyard. There are also no additional benefits no matter how many cards are in an opponent’s graveyard, as long as there are at least eight.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a multiplayer game, once an opponent leaves the game, they won’t be considered for such an effect, no matter how many cards they had in their graveyard before leaving the game.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a creature becomes the target of a spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger. It resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature without a +1/+1 counter on it becomes the target of a spell an opponent controls, putting a +1/+1 counter on it after that won’t cause Swarm Shambler’s middle ability to trigger.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a spell targets a creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it more than once, Swarm Shambler’s ability triggers only once.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You create just one Insect token, no matter how many +1/+1 counters the target creature has on it.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a permanent becomes the target of a spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger. It resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a kicked spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell. It resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a spell targets Myriad Construct more than once, its last ability triggers only once.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you copy a kicked spell, the copy is also kicked. If a card or token enters the battlefield as a copy of a permanent that’s already on the battlefield, the new permanent isn’t kicked, even if the original was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you don’t sacrifice Myriad Construct as its last ability resolves (perhaps because its ability triggered more than once and you’ve already sacrificed it), you still create Construct tokens. The number of tokens you create is determined by Myriad Construct’s power as it last existed on the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can’t kick it.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Kicker represents an optional additional cost that you may choose to pay as you cast the spell. A spell cast with that additional cost paid is “kicked.”'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Some instant or sorcery spells require alternative or additional targets if they’re kicked. You ignore these targeting requirements if those spells aren’t kicked, and you can’t kick those spells unless you can choose the appropriate targets. On the other hand, you can kick a permanent spell even if you won’t be able to choose targets for an enters-the-battlefield ability of that permanent once the spell resolves.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine a spell’s total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card’s effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The converted mana cost of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can’t pay a kicker cost more than once.'}]", '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'An ability that triggers when a player casts a kicked spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell. It resolves even if that spell is countered.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If any abilities trigger when the lands are put onto the battlefield and Vastwood Surge was kicked, those abilities won\'t resolve until after you\'ve put two +1/+1 counters on creatures you control."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If you copy a kicked spell, the copy is also kicked. If a card or token enters the battlefield as a copy of a permanent that\'s already on the battlefield, the new permanent isn\'t kicked, even if the original was."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can\'t kick it."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'Kicker represents an optional additional cost that you may choose to pay as you cast the spell. A spell cast with that additional cost paid is “kicked.”\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Some instant or sorcery spells require alternative or additional targets if they\'re kicked. You ignore these targeting requirements if those spells aren\'t kicked, and you can\'t kick those spells unless you can choose the appropriate targets. On the other hand, you can kick a permanent spell even if you won\'t be able to choose targets for an enters-the-battlefield ability of that permanent once the spell resolves."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "To determine a spell\'s total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card\'s effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "You can\'t pay a kicker cost more than once."}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'An ability that triggers when a player casts a kicked spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell. It resolves even if that spell is countered.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If the Equipment can\'t be attached to Thieving Skydiver, most likely because Thieving Skydiver has left the battlefield before its triggered ability resolves, the Equipment remains attached to whatever it\'s currently attached to or remains unattached if attached to nothing."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If you copy a kicked spell, the copy is also kicked. If a card or token enters the battlefield as a copy of a permanent that\'s already on the battlefield, the new permanent isn\'t kicked, even if the original was."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can\'t kick it."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'Kicker represents an optional additional cost that you may choose to pay as you cast the spell. A spell cast with that additional cost paid is "kicked."\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Some instant or sorcery spells require alternative or additional targets if they\'re kicked. You ignore these targeting requirements if those spells aren\'t kicked, and you can\'t kick those spells unless you can choose the appropriate targets. On the other hand, you can kick a permanent spell even if you won\'t be able to choose targets for an enters-the-battlefield ability of that permanent once the spell resolves."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "The control-change effect of Thieving Skydiver lasts indefinitely. It doesn\'t wear off during the cleanup step, and it doesn\'t expire if Thieving Skydiver leaves the battlefield. In a multiplayer game, it does expire if you leave the game."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Thieving Skydiver\'s ability can target an artifact you already control. You\'ll attach it to Thieving Skydiver if it\'s an Equipment."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "To determine a spell\'s total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card\'s effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "You can\'t pay a kicker cost more than once."}]', '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'An ability that triggers when a player casts a kicked spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell. It resolves even if that spell is countered.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If you copy a kicked spell, the copy is also kicked. If a card or token enters the battlefield as a copy of a permanent that\'s already on the battlefield, the new permanent isn\'t kicked, even if the original was."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can\'t kick it."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'Kicker represents an optional additional cost that you may choose to pay as you cast the spell. A spell cast with that additional cost paid is “kicked.”\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Some instant or sorcery spells require alternative or additional targets if they\'re kicked. You ignore these targeting requirements if those spells aren\'t kicked, and you can\'t kick those spells unless you can choose the appropriate targets. On the other hand, you can kick a permanent spell even if you won\'t be able to choose targets for an enters-the-battlefield ability of that permanent once the spell resolves."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "To determine a spell\'s total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card\'s effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "You can\'t pay a kicker cost more than once."}]', "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a kicked spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell. It resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger. It resolves even if that spell is countered. Notably, Scourge of the Skyclaves may have its toughness change from less than 0 to greater than 0 as a result of its triggered ability before it resolves and enters the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the highest life total among players is greater than 20, Scourge of the Skyclaves has negative power and toughness equal to the difference.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you copy a kicked spell, the copy is also kicked. If a card or token enters the battlefield as a copy of a permanent that’s already on the battlefield, the new permanent isn’t kicked, even if the original was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can’t kick it.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a Two-Headed Giant game, Scourge of the Skyclaves causes each team to lose twice half their life rounded up, which is their full life total or, if it’s odd, that much life plus 1. This causes the game to end in a draw.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Kicker represents an optional additional cost that you may choose to pay as you cast the spell. A spell cast with that additional cost paid is “kicked.”'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Some instant or sorcery spells require alternative or additional targets if they’re kicked. You ignore these targeting requirements if those spells aren’t kicked, and you can’t kick those spells unless you can choose the appropriate targets. On the other hand, you can kick a permanent spell even if you won’t be able to choose targets for an enters-the-battlefield ability of that permanent once the spell resolves.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The ability that defines Scourge of the Skyclaves’s power and toughness applies in all zones, not just the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine a spell’s total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card’s effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The converted mana cost of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can’t pay a kicker cost more than once.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a kicked spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell. It resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Because targets are chosen as you cast a spell, you can’t have Inscription of Ruin return a creature card and then destroy that creature.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a card in a player’s graveyard or a creature on the battlefield has {X} in its mana cost, X is considered to be 0.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If any targets become illegal, the other targets will still be affected as appropriate.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If more than one mode is chosen, perform them in the order written. Nothing can happen in between, however, and no player may choose to take actions. Any abilities that trigger will be put onto the stack after the spell has finished resolving.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you copy a kicked spell, the copy is also kicked. If a card or token enters the battlefield as a copy of a permanent that’s already on the battlefield, the new permanent isn’t kicked, even if the original was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you kick Inscription of Ruin, you can’t choose any one mode more than once.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can’t kick it.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Kicker represents an optional additional cost that you may choose to pay as you cast the spell. A spell cast with that additional cost paid is “kicked.”'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Some instant or sorcery spells require alternative or additional targets if they’re kicked. You ignore these targeting requirements if those spells aren’t kicked, and you can’t kick those spells unless you can choose the appropriate targets. On the other hand, you can kick a permanent spell even if you won’t be able to choose targets for an enters-the-battlefield ability of that permanent once the spell resolves.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine a spell’s total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card’s effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The converted mana cost of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can’t pay a kicker cost more than once.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a kicked spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell. It resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If Tajuru Paragon leaves the battlefield before its triggered ability resolves, use its creature types as it last existed on the battlefield to determine which cards you may put into your hand.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you copy a kicked spell, the copy is also kicked. If a card or token enters the battlefield as a copy of a permanent that’s already on the battlefield, the new permanent isn’t kicked, even if the original was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can’t kick it.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Kicker represents an optional additional cost that you may choose to pay as you cast the spell. A spell cast with that additional cost paid is “kicked.”'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Some instant or sorcery spells require alternative or additional targets if they’re kicked. You ignore these targeting requirements if those spells aren’t kicked, and you can’t kick those spells unless you can choose the appropriate targets. On the other hand, you can kick a permanent spell even if you won’t be able to choose targets for an enters-the-battlefield ability of that permanent once the spell resolves.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The ability that adds creature types to Tajuru Paragon applies in all zones, not just the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine a spell’s total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card’s effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The converted mana cost of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can’t pay a kicker cost more than once.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a kicked spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell. It resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a card in a player’s hand has {X} in its mana cost, X is considered to be 0.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the card draw from Jace’s last ability is modified by a replacement effect, you don’t reveal any card, even if the draw was replaced by one or more card draws. No loyalty counters will be removed from Jace in that case.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the converted mana cost of the drawn card is greater than Jace’s loyalty, you remove all loyalty counters from him. He’ll be put into your graveyard as a state-based action before you can take any actions.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you copy a kicked spell, the copy is also kicked. If a card or token enters the battlefield as a copy of a permanent that’s already on the battlefield, the new permanent isn’t kicked, even if the original was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can’t kick it.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Kicker represents an optional additional cost that you may choose to pay as you cast the spell. A spell cast with that additional cost paid is “kicked.”'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Some instant or sorcery spells require alternative or additional targets if they’re kicked. You ignore these targeting requirements if those spells aren’t kicked, and you can’t kick those spells unless you can choose the appropriate targets. On the other hand, you can kick a permanent spell even if you won’t be able to choose targets for an enters-the-battlefield ability of that permanent once the spell resolves.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The token created by Jace’s triggered ability doesn’t have the legendary supertype and has a starting loyalty of 1 rather than 4. If another object becomes a copy of the token, that copy also won’t be legendary and will have a starting loyalty of 1.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The token from Jace’s triggered ability copies exactly what is printed on Jace and nothing else. It doesn’t copy how many counters are on him, or any non-copy effects that have changed his color or types, and so on. It enters the battlefield with one loyalty counter. You can activate one loyalty ability of each of the Jaces this turn.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine a spell’s total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card’s effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The converted mana cost of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'While resolving Jace’s last ability, you must reveal the card before it’s mixed with the other cards in your hand.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can control one legendary Jace, Mirror Mage in addition to any number of nonlegendary copies of Jace, Mirror Mage.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can’t pay a kicker cost more than once.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a kicked spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell. It resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature the defending player controls can’t block the target creature for any reason (such as being tapped), then it doesn’t block that creature. If there’s a cost associated with having a creature block the attacking creature, the defending player isn’t forced to pay that cost, so it doesn’t have to block in that case either.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you copy a kicked spell, the copy is also kicked. If a card or token enters the battlefield as a copy of a permanent that’s already on the battlefield, the new permanent isn’t kicked, even if the original was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can’t kick it.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Kicker represents an optional additional cost that you may choose to pay as you cast the spell. A spell cast with that additional cost paid is “kicked.”'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Some instant or sorcery spells require alternative or additional targets if they’re kicked. You ignore these targeting requirements if those spells aren’t kicked, and you can’t kick those spells unless you can choose the appropriate targets. On the other hand, you can kick a permanent spell even if you won’t be able to choose targets for an enters-the-battlefield ability of that permanent once the spell resolves.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine a spell’s total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card’s effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The converted mana cost of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can’t pay a kicker cost more than once.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a kicked spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell. It resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If any targets become illegal, the other targets will still be affected as appropriate. If any targets are chosen and every target becomes illegal, Inscription of Insight doesn’t resolve. You won’t scry 2 or draw two cards if the middle mode was chosen.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If more than one mode is chosen, perform them in the order written. Nothing can happen in between, however, and no player may choose to take actions. Any abilities that trigger will be put onto the stack after the spell has finished resolving.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you copy a kicked spell, the copy is also kicked. If a card or token enters the battlefield as a copy of a permanent that’s already on the battlefield, the new permanent isn’t kicked, even if the original was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you kick Inscription of Insight, you can’t choose any one mode more than once.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can’t kick it.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Kicker represents an optional additional cost that you may choose to pay as you cast the spell. A spell cast with that additional cost paid is “kicked.”'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Some instant or sorcery spells require alternative or additional targets if they’re kicked. You ignore these targeting requirements if those spells aren’t kicked, and you can’t kick those spells unless you can choose the appropriate targets. On the other hand, you can kick a permanent spell even if you won’t be able to choose targets for an enters-the-battlefield ability of that permanent once the spell resolves.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The value of X is determined only as you perform the third mode while Inscription of Insight is resolving. Once that happens, the value of X won’t change even if the number of cards in the player’s hand changes.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine a spell’s total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card’s effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The converted mana cost of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can’t pay a kicker cost more than once.'}]", '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'An ability that triggers when a player casts a kicked spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell. It resolves even if that spell is countered.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'If any targets become illegal, the other targets will still be affected as appropriate.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'If either target creature is an illegal target as Inscription of Abundance resolves with its last mode chosen, no creature will deal or be dealt damage.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'If more than one mode is chosen, perform them in the order written. Nothing can happen in between, however, and no player may choose to take actions. Any abilities that trigger will be put onto the stack after the spell has finished resolving.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If the second mode is chosen and each creature the target player controls has negative power, that player doesn\'t gain or lose life."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If you copy a kicked spell, the copy is also kicked. If a card or token enters the battlefield as a copy of a permanent that\'s already on the battlefield, the new permanent isn\'t kicked, even if the original was."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If you kick Inscription of Abundance, you can\'t choose any one mode more than once."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can\'t kick it."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'Kicker represents an optional additional cost that you may choose to pay as you cast the spell. A spell cast with that additional cost paid is "kicked."\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Some instant or sorcery spells require alternative or additional targets if they\'re kicked. You ignore these targeting requirements if those spells aren\'t kicked, and you can\'t kick those spells unless you can choose the appropriate targets. On the other hand, you can kick a permanent spell even if you won\'t be able to choose targets for an enters-the-battlefield ability of that permanent once the spell resolves."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "To determine a spell\'s total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card\'s effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "You can\'t pay a kicker cost more than once."}]', "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a kicked spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell. It resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you copy a kicked spell, the copy is also kicked. If a card or token enters the battlefield as a copy of a permanent that’s already on the battlefield, the new permanent isn’t kicked, even if the original was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can’t kick it.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Kicker represents an optional additional cost that you may choose to pay as you cast the spell. A spell cast with that additional cost paid is “kicked.”'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Moss-Pit Skeleton’s last ability triggers if a creature enters the battlefield under your control with +1/+1 counters on it, as well as when +1/+1 counters are put on a creature you already control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Moss-Pit Skeleton’s last ability triggers only if it’s already in your graveyard as +1/+1 counters are put onto a creature you control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Some instant or sorcery spells require alternative or additional targets if they’re kicked. You ignore these targeting requirements if those spells aren’t kicked, and you can’t kick those spells unless you can choose the appropriate targets. On the other hand, you can kick a permanent spell even if you won’t be able to choose targets for an enters-the-battlefield ability of that permanent once the spell resolves.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine a spell’s total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card’s effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The converted mana cost of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can’t pay a kicker cost more than once.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a kicked spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell. It resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you copy a kicked spell, the copy is also kicked. If a card or token enters the battlefield as a copy of a permanent that’s already on the battlefield, the new permanent isn’t kicked, even if the original was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can’t kick it.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Kicker represents an optional additional cost that you may choose to pay as you cast the spell. A spell cast with that additional cost paid is “kicked.”'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Some instant or sorcery spells require alternative or additional targets if they’re kicked. You ignore these targeting requirements if those spells aren’t kicked, and you can’t kick those spells unless you can choose the appropriate targets. On the other hand, you can kick a permanent spell even if you won’t be able to choose targets for an enters-the-battlefield ability of that permanent once the spell resolves.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine a spell’s total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card’s effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The converted mana cost of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can’t pay a kicker cost more than once.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when a player casts a kicked spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger, but after targets have been chosen for that spell. It resolves even if that spell is countered.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you copy a kicked spell, the copy is also kicked. If a card or token enters the battlefield as a copy of a permanent that’s already on the battlefield, the new permanent isn’t kicked, even if the original was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can’t kick it.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Kicker represents an optional additional cost that you may choose to pay as you cast the spell. A spell cast with that additional cost paid is “kicked.”'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Some instant or sorcery spells require alternative or additional targets if they’re kicked. You ignore these targeting requirements if those spells aren’t kicked, and you can’t kick those spells unless you can choose the appropriate targets. On the other hand, you can kick a permanent spell even if you won’t be able to choose targets for an enters-the-battlefield ability of that permanent once the spell resolves.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine a spell’s total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card’s effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can’t pay a kicker cost more than once.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers whenever you gain life “for the first time each turn” won’t trigger if you gain life during a turn before the permanent with that ability is on the battlefield, even if you gain life again later in the turn.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers “whenever you gain life” triggers just once for each life-gaining event, no matter how much life you gain.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Each creature with lifelink dealing combat damage causes a separate life-gaining event. For example, if two creatures you control with lifelink deal combat damage at the same time, a “whenever you gain life” ability will trigger twice. However, if a single creature you control with lifelink deals combat damage to multiple creatures, players, and/or planeswalkers at the same time (perhaps because it has trample or was blocked by more than one creature), the ability will trigger only once.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you gain an amount of life “for each” of something, that life is gained as one event and the ability will trigger only once.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a Two-Headed Giant game, life gained by your teammate won’t cause the ability to trigger, even though it caused your team’s life total to increase.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Multiple instances of lifelink on the same creature are redundant.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers whenever you gain life “for the first time each turn” won’t trigger if you gain life during a turn before the permanent with that ability is on the battlefield, even if you gain life again later in the turn.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers “whenever you gain life” triggers just once for each life-gaining event, no matter how much life you gain.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Each creature with lifelink dealing combat damage causes a separate life-gaining event. For example, if two creatures you control with lifelink deal combat damage at the same time, a “whenever you gain life” ability will trigger twice. However, if a single creature you control with lifelink deals combat damage to multiple creatures, players, and/or planeswalkers at the same time (perhaps because it has trample or was blocked by more than one creature), the ability will trigger only once.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you gain an amount of life “for each” of something, that life is gained as one event and the ability will trigger only once.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a Two-Headed Giant game, life gained by your teammate won’t cause the ability to trigger, even though it caused your team’s life total to increase.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers “whenever you gain life” triggers just once for each life-gaining event, no matter how much life you gain.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Each creature with lifelink dealing combat damage causes a separate life-gaining event. For example, if two creatures you control with lifelink deal combat damage at the same time, a “whenever you gain life” ability will trigger twice. However, if a single creature you control with lifelink deals combat damage to multiple creatures, players, and/or planeswalkers at the same time (perhaps because it has trample or was blocked by more than one creature), the ability will trigger only once.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you gain an amount of life “for each” of something, that life is gained as one event and the ability will trigger only once.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you gain life at the same time Scion of the Swarm is dealt lethal damage, it dies before its ability can put a +1/+1 counter on it.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a Two-Headed Giant game, life gained by your teammate won’t cause the ability to trigger, even though it caused your team’s life total to increase.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An ability that triggers “whenever you gain life” triggers just once for each life-gaining event, no matter how much life you gain.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Each creature with lifelink dealing combat damage causes a separate life-gaining event. For example, if two creatures you control with lifelink deal combat damage at the same time, a “whenever you gain life” ability will trigger twice. However, if a single creature you control with lifelink deals combat damage to multiple creatures, players, and/or planeswalkers at the same time (perhaps because it has trample or was blocked by more than one creature), the ability will trigger only once.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you gain an amount of life “for each” of something, that life is gained as one event and the ability will trigger only once.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a Two-Headed Giant game, Marauding Blight-Priest’s ability causes the opposing team to lose 2 life.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a Two-Headed Giant game, life gained by your teammate won’t cause the ability to trigger, even though it caused your team’s life total to increase.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'An opponent’s spell that targets Charix more than once costs only {2} more to cast.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Each time you activate Charix’s last ability, the value of X for that instance of the ability is determined only as that ability resolves. Once that happens, the size of the power-and-toughness change for that instance of the ability won’t change later in the turn, even if the number of Islands you control does change.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost you’re paying, add any cost increases (such as that of Charix), then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Archon of Emeria looks at the entire turn to see if a player has cast a spell, even if Archon of Emeria wasn’t on the battlefield when that spell was cast. Notably, you can’t cast Archon of Emeria and then cast another spell during the same turn.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect says that a land enters tapped unless a condition is met or a cost is paid, that land enters tapped even if that condition is met or that cost is paid if it’s affected by Archon of Emeria’s second ability.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you cast a spell that was countered, you can’t cast another spell during the same turn.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'As Soul Shatter resolves, first the opponent whose turn it is (or the next opponent in turn order, if it’s your turn) chooses a creature or planeswalker they control with the highest converted mana cost among that player’s creatures and planeswalkers, then each other opponent in turn order does the same, knowing the choices made before them. Then all of the chosen permanents are sacrificed at the same time.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Attaching an Equipment with its enters-the-battlefield triggered ability isn’t the same as using its equip ability. You don’t pay mana for the attachment, and if the Equipment enters at a time you couldn’t cast a sorcery, you can still attach it to a creature you control.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the target creature becomes an illegal target, the Equipment remains on the battlefield unattached.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Because all attackers are declared at the same time, the returned creature can’t attack during the same combat it returns, even if it has haste.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If Drana attacks a planeswalker, that planeswalker’s controller is the defending player.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The defending player chooses a card and you put it onto the battlefield all while Drana’s ability is resolving. No player may take actions in between those events.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The returned creature remains a Vampire in addition to its other types even after Drana leaves the battlefield.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Because damage remains marked on a creature until the damage is removed as the turn ends, nonlethal damage dealt to another Warrior you control may become lethal if Kargan Warleader leaves the battlefield during that turn.'}]", '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'Card types that can appear on cards in a graveyard include artifact, creature, enchantment, instant, land, planeswalker, and sorcery. Legendary, basic, and snow are supertypes, not card types; Vampire and Rogue are subtypes, not card types.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "Nighthawk Scavenger counts card types, not cards. If the only card in your opponents\' graveyards is a single artifact creature card, Nighthawk Scavenger will be 3/3. If the only cards in those graveyards are ten artifact cards and ten creature cards, Nighthawk Scavenger will still be 3/3."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "The ability that defines Nighthawk Scavenger\'s power applies in all zones, not just the battlefield."}]', "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Colorless mana won’t give Springmantle Cleric another +1/+1 counter. Colorless is not a color.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If Springmantle Cleric enters the battlefield without being cast, it receives no +1/+1 counters.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an effect allows you to spend mana as though it were mana of any color to cast Springmantle Cleric, you consider only the actual mana spent to determine how many counters it receives.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If another creature enters the battlefield as a copy of Springmantle Cleric, consider what mana was spent to cast that creature to determine how many +1/+1 counters it enters with.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Dauntless Survivor can be the target of its own ability.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Destroying a blocking creature doesn’t cause the creature it was blocking to become unblocked.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Sizzling Barrage can target a creature that’s currently blocking or one that blocked earlier in the turn and is no longer blocking.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Effects that modify Risen Riptide’s power or toughness without setting it will apply to its new base power and toughness no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for counters that change the creature’s power or toughness.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Risen Riptide’s ability overwrites any previous effects that set its power and/or toughness to specific values. Other effects that set these characteristics to specific values that start to apply after the ability resolves will overwrite that part of the effect.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Expedition Champion gets just +2/+0, no matter how many other Warriors you control beyond the first.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Expedition Diviner has just one instance of its triggered ability, no matter how many other Wizards you control beyond the first.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If Expedition Diviner dies at the same time that each other Wizard you control leaves the battlefield, its ability triggers. For example, if the only creatures you control are two Expedition Diviners and both die at the same time, their abilities each trigger.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Fireblade Charger’s last known existence on the battlefield is checked to determine its power. If its power was 0 or negative, its ability has no effect.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Grakmaw’s second ability puts just one +1/+1 counter on it, no matter how many counters the dying creature had.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature with a +1/+1 counter on it dies after receiving too many -1/-1 counters, it dies at the same time that the counters are removed, and Grakmaw’s second ability triggers. Similarly, if Grakmaw dies after receiving too many -1/-1 counters, use the number of +1/+1 counters it had prior to receiving the -1/-1 counters to determine the value of X.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If Farsight Adept’s ability can’t legally target an opponent, or if the ability’s target becomes illegal while the ability is on the stack, you don’t draw a card.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If Iridescent Hornbeetle leaves the battlefield before your end step, its ability won’t trigger at all. You won’t create any tokens.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature enters the battlefield under your control with +1/+1 counters on it, Iridescent Hornbeetle’s ability counts those counters.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Iridescent Hornbeetle’s ability counts the number of +1/+1 counters you’ve put on your creatures, even if that happened before Iridescent Hornbeetle was on the battlefield, and even if those creatures are no longer on the battlefield or under your control (and, in some rare cases, even if those creatures aren’t creatures anymore).'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If Relic Vial leaves the battlefield at the same time as each Cleric you control, the triggered ability triggers for any creatures you control that die at the same time (possibly including those Clerics).'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you sacrifice the only Cleric you control to activate Relic Vial’s first ability, the triggered ability it gives itself triggers.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a Two-Headed Giant game, Relic Vial’s ability causes the opposing team to lose 2 life and you to gain 1 life.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Once Relic Vial’s ability has triggered, that ability resolves even if you no longer control a Cleric.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If Skyclave Apparition leaves the battlefield before its first ability resolves, the ability still exiles the target permanent.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If Skyclave Apparition’s first ability exiled more than one card owned by a single player, that player creates a token with power and toughness equal to the sum of those cards’ converted mana costs. If the first ability exiled cards owned by more than one player, each of those players creates a token with power and toughness equal to the sum of the converted mana costs of all cards exiled by the first ability.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature on the battlefield has {X} in its mana cost, X is considered to be 0.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If there’s no exiled card when Skyclave Apparition leaves the battlefield (most likely because its first ability hasn’t resolved yet), no player creates a token.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If Skyclave Shadowcat dies at the same time as another creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it, its last ability triggers for that creature.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If Skyclave Shadowcat has a +1/+1 counter on it and it dies, its last ability triggers.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature with a +1/+1 counter on it died due to receiving too many -1/-1 counters, it dies at the same time that the counters are removed, and Skyclave Shadowcat’s last ability triggers.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You draw just one card each time Skyclave Shadowcat’s last ability resolves, no matter how many +1/+1 counters the creature had on it.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature loses double strike after assigning damage in the first strike combat damage step (due to Kor Blademaster leaving the battlefield, for example), that creature won’t assign damage in the normal combat damage step.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a creature on the battlefield or a creature card in a graveyard has {X} in its mana cost, X is considered to be 0.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If another Cleric you control dies at the same time as Orah, Orah’s ability triggers for that Cleric in addition to triggering for itself.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Orah’s ability can target a Cleric card that was put into your graveyard at the same time as the Cleric whose death caused the ability to trigger.'}]", '[{\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': \'If a permanent on the battlefield has {X} in its mana cost, X is considered to be 0.\'}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "If the target permanent is an illegal target by the time Feed the Swarm tries to resolve, the spell doesn\'t resolve. You don\'t lose any life. If the target is legal but not destroyed (most likely because it has indestructible), you do lose life."}, {\'date\': \'2020-09-25\', \'text\': "The amount of life you lose is determined by the permanent\'s mana value as it last existed on the battlefield."}]', "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a red mana you add to your mana pool has certain restrictions or riders associated with it (for example, if it was produced by Base Camp), they’ll apply to that mana no matter when you spend it.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Leyline Tyrant’s last ability goes on the stack without a target. While that ability is resolving, you may pay any amount of red mana, including from the unspent mana you have. If you do, a second ability triggers and you pick one target to be dealt that much damage. This is different from abilities that say “If you do . . .” in that players may cast spells and activate abilities after mana is paid but before the damage is dealt.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Once Leyline Tyrant leaves the battlefield, you have until the end of the current step or phase to spend whatever red mana is in your mana pool before it empties as normal. There is no penalty associated with this other than the loss of the mana.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can keep red mana in your mana pool indefinitely while Leyline Tyrant is on the battlefield. That means if you add a red mana to your mana pool during one step or phase, you can spend it during a later step or phase, or even a later turn. Other types of mana will continue to empty from your mana pool as each step and phase ends.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If a spell or activated ability has a cost that requires a player to pay life (such as the activated ability granted by Lithoform Blight) or sacrifice a permanent (such as Kazuul’s Fury or Spare Supplies), that spell or ability can’t be cast or activated.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Other things may still cause players to pay life or sacrifice creatures, such as a resolving spell or ability.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Yasharn’s first ability can find just one basic Forest or one basic Plains card if you don’t have both in your library or if you don’t wish to find both.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If an opponent has had no lands enter under their control and then two or more lands enter at the same time, Confounding Conundrum’s second ability triggers for each of those lands.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The player may return any land they control to its owner’s hand, not just one of those that entered this turn.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the blocked creature is untapped (most likely because it has vigilance), the ability doesn’t tap it.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The blocked creature doesn’t untap even if Cleric of Chill Depths leaves the battlefield before that creature’s controller’s next upkeep.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the target creature is an illegal target by the time Chilling Trap tries to resolve, the spell doesn’t resolve. You don’t draw a card if you control a Wizard.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the target creature is an illegal target by the time Glacial Grasp tries to resolve, the spell doesn’t resolve. No player mills or draws any cards, and the creature won’t be stopped from untapping. If the target is legal but Glacial Grasp doesn’t tap it (most likely because it’s already tapped), the rest of Glacial Grasp’s effects still happen: that creature won’t untap during its controller’s next untap step, that player mills two cards, and you draw a card.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the target creature is an illegal target by the time Inordinate Rage tries to resolve, the spell doesn’t resolve. You don’t scry 1.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the target creature is an illegal target by the time Zulaport Duelist’s ability tries to resolve, the ability doesn’t resolve. No player mills two cards.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the target creature’s power is greater than 2 as Sneaking Guide’s ability tries to resolve, the ability doesn’t resolve. However, if instead the creature’s power is raised above 2 after the ability resolves, it still can’t be blocked that turn.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Once a creature with power 2 or less has been blocked, Sneaking Guide’s ability won’t cause it to become unblocked.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the target land is an illegal target by the time Cleansing Wildfire tries to resolve, the spell doesn’t resolve. No player searches for a basic land card and you don’t draw a card. If the target is legal but not destroyed (most likely because it has indestructible), its controller does search for a basic land card and you do draw a card.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the target land is an illegal target by the time Lithoform Blight tries to resolve, the spell doesn’t resolve. It doesn’t enter the battlefield, so you don’t draw a card.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The enchanted land keeps any other card types (such as artifact) and supertypes (such as basic or legendary) when it loses its land types.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If the target opponent can discard only one card or can’t discard any cards, they still mill a card and lose 1 life, and you gain 1 life.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you choose a target creature and it’s an illegal target by the time Scale the Heights tries to resolve, the spell doesn’t resolve. You don’t gain life, draw a card, or get to play an additional land.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The permission to play lands is cumulative with other effects that allow you to play additional lands, such as that of Nahiri’s Lithoforming.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You don’t play a land as Scale the Heights resolves; Scale the Heights fully resolves first and you draw a card, perhaps including a land you’ll play later. If it’s not your turn, you won’t be able to play a land this turn at all.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you choose both modes and one target becomes illegal before Subtle Strike resolves, the other target is affected as appropriate.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you control two or more Kargan Intimidators, track which modes have been chosen each turn for each one’s ability separately.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Once a creature has blocked a Warrior, turning that creature into a Coward won’t remove it from combat or cause the Warrior to become unblocked.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you don’t play the exiled card you chose, it remains exiled. The card you didn’t choose remains exiled whether you play the chosen card or not.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Magmatic Channeler gets just +3/+1 from its first ability, no matter how many instant and sorcery cards are in your graveyard beyond the fourth.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You choose which card you’ll be allowed to play this turn while Magmatic Channeler’s ability is resolving, but you must follow the normal timing permissions and restrictions for the card when you play it. If it’s a land, you can’t play it unless you have land plays available.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You’ll still pay all costs for a spell cast this way, including additional costs. You may also pay alternative costs if any are available.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you don’t play the exiled card, it remains exiled.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You must follow the normal timing permissions and restrictions for the exiled card. If it’s a land, you can’t play it unless you have land plays available.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You’ll still pay all costs for a spell cast this way, including additional costs. You may also pay alternative costs if any are available.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'If you draw a card this way, that card is the next one in your library after putting the five cards from the top of your library on the bottom.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a Two-Headed Giant game, Pyroclastic Hellion’s ability causes the opposing team to lose 4 life.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'While resolving Pyroclastic Hellion’s ability, you can’t return more than one land to have it deal more damage.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a casual game, a card you choose from outside the game comes from your personal collection. In a tournament event, a card you choose from outside the game must come from your sideboard. You may look at your sideboard any time.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'In a casual game, you may find a Legion Angel outside the game even if your deck contains already four copies of Legion Angel. In a Constructed tournament event, you can’t have more than four copies of Legion Angel between your deck and sideboard.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Luminarch Aspirant can be the target of its own ability.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Multiple instances of menace on the same creature are redundant.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Murasa Rootgrazer’s middle ability doesn’t count as playing a land. It can put a land card onto the battlefield even if you’ve already played your land for the turn.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Once Murasa Rootgrazer has attacked, you can activate either of its activated abilities. Doing so doesn’t remove it from combat. It remains an attacking creature and will deal and receive combat damage as normal.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Once a creature has blocked Sure-Footed Infiltrator, activating its first ability won’t cause it to become unblocked or remove that blocking creature from combat.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can tap any other untapped Rogue you control, including one you haven’t controlled continuously since the beginning of your most recent turn, to pay the cost of Sure-Footed Infiltrator’s first ability.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Oran-Rief Ooze can be the target of its own first ability.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The group of creatures that receive a +1/+1 counter from Oran-Rief Ooze’s second ability is determined only as the ability resolves. Other abilities that trigger on attacking (such as that of Paired Tactician) may add counters to creatures before that ability resolves.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'Paired Tactician gets just one +1/+1 counter from its ability, no matter how many Warriors attack with it beyond the first.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The other attacking Warrior doesn’t have to be attacking the same player or planeswalker as Paired Tactician.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The ability that adds creature types to Stonework Packbeast applies in all zones, not just the battlefield.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The mana generated by Base Camp’s last ability can’t be spent to activate abilities of cards that aren’t on the battlefield or to pay a cost in a resolving triggered ability.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The power of the target creature and the number of Warriors you control are checked only as Goma Fada Vanguard’s ability is put onto the stack and as that ability resolves. If the creature’s power becomes greater after the ability has resolved, it still can’t block.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'The target creature is restricted from blocking anything, not just Goma Fada Vanguard.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'While resolving Fissure Wizard’s ability, you can’t discard more than one card.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You can tap any other untapped Rogue you control, including one you haven’t controlled continuously since the beginning of your most recent turn, to pay the cost of Shadow Stinger’s first ability.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You create a Kor Warrior token and attach an Equipment to it if you wish all while Nahiri’s first ability is resolving. Nothing can happen in between, and no player may choose to take actions.'}]", "[{'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': 'You draw a card and discard a card while Coralhelm Chronicler’s first ability is resolving. No player may take actions between those events, and nothing can happen.'}, {'date': '2020-09-25', 'text': '“A kicker ability” includes the multikicker variant, which doesn’t appear in Zendikar Rising. If you cast a spell with multikicker, the first ability will trigger only once, no matter how many times you kicked the spell.'}]"]
foreign_names: ['[{\'name\': \'Abtrünnige Lotsen-Bestie\', \'text\': \'Verursacht Trampelschaden, Eile\\nImmer wenn die Abtrünnige Lotsen-Bestie einem Spieler Kampfschaden zufügt, bringe ein Land, das du kontrollierst, auf die Hand seines Besitzers zurück.\', \'type\': \'Kreatur — Bestie\', \'flavor\': \'Die Taktik der Goblin-Kavallerie besteht darin, eine Bestie in eine Richtung zu lenken und sich so lange wie möglich daran festzuhalten.\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492137&type=card\', \'language\': \'German\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'180e9798-ab09-4a92-bf16-bf39b37c1a4f\', \'multiverseId\': 492137}, \'multiverseid\': 492137}, {\'name\': \'Bestia guía rebelde\', \'text\': \'Arrolla, prisa.\\nSiempre que la Bestia guía rebelde haga daño de combate a un jugador, regresa una tierra que controlas a la mano de su propietario.\', \'type\': \'Criatura — Bestia\', \'flavor\': \'Las tácticas de caballería trasgas consisten en apuntar a la bestia en una dirección y sujetarse lo máximo posible.\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492453&type=card\', \'language\': \'Spanish\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'3aaf76b4-dade-4e49-84db-4f8ef221ce02\', \'multiverseId\': 492453}, \'multiverseid\': 492453}, {\'name\': \'Bête-guide rétive\', \'text\': \'Piétinement, célérité\\nÀ chaque fois que la Bête-guide rétive inflige des blessures de combat à un joueur, renvoyez un terrain que vous contrôlez dans la main de son propriétaire.\', \'type\': \'Créature : bête\', \'flavor\': "La tactique de la cavalerie gobeline consiste à pointer une bête dans une direction et à s\'accrocher aussi longtemps que possible.", \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492769&type=card\', \'language\': \'French\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'1fca241b-38d5-40ee-b40b-28d1c76ed8ea\', \'multiverseId\': 492769}, \'multiverseid\': 492769}, {\'name\': \'Bestia-Guida Fuori Controllo\', \'text\': \'Travolgere, rapidità\\nOgniqualvolta la Bestia-Guida Fuori Controllo infligge danno da combattimento a un giocatore, fai tornare una terra che controlli in mano al suo proprietario.\', \'type\': \'Creatura — Bestia\', \'flavor\': \'La tattica della cavalleria goblin consiste nel puntare una bestia in una direzione e resistere in sella il più a lungo possibile.\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493085&type=card\', \'language\': \'Italian\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'003bc001-1fb0-44bd-9197-71b02cf15f91\', \'multiverseId\': 493085}, \'multiverseid\': 493085}, {\'name\': \'むら気な猛導獣\', \'text\': \'トランプル、速攻\\nむら気な猛導獣がプレイヤー１人に戦闘ダメージを与えるたび、あなたがコントロールしている土地１つをオーナーの手札に戻す。\', \'type\': \'クリーチャー — ビースト\', \'flavor\': \'ゴブリン騎兵の戦術は、獣に向きを示すことと、できるかぎり長くしがみついていることからなる。\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493401&type=card\', \'language\': \'Japanese\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'c5b40e58-562a-45f0-ab5f-1499d11daf8c\', \'multiverseId\': 493401}, \'multiverseid\': 493401}, {\'name\': \'고집센 안내야수\', \'text\': \'돌진, 신속\\n고집센 안내야수가 플레이어에게 전투피해를 입힐 때마다, 당신이 조종하는 대지 한 개를 소유자의 손으로 되돌린다.\', \'type\': \'생물 — 야수\', \'flavor\': \'고블린 기병대의 전술은 야수를 한쪽 방향으로 보게 한 다음 거기에 최대한 매달려 있는 것이다.\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493717&type=card\', \'language\': \'Korean\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'83cfc4b8-042d-4748-8503-420b913a9c11\', \'multiverseId\': 493717}, \'multiverseid\': 493717}, {\'name\': \'Fera-guia Errática\', \'text\': \'Atropelar, ímpeto\\nToda vez que Fera-guia Errática causar dano de combate a um jogador, devolva um terreno que você controla para a mão de seu dono.\', \'type\': \'Criatura — Besta\', \'flavor\': \'A tática de cavalaria dos goblins consiste em direcionar a fera e segui-la pelo maior tempo possível.\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494033&type=card\', \'language\': \'Portuguese (Brazil)\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'3860e43e-e625-43f0-b81a-187de9eaf6d0\', \'multiverseId\': 494033}, \'multiverseid\': 494033}, {\'name\': \'Своенравный Зверь-Поводырь\', \'text\': \'Пробивной удар, Ускорение\\nКаждый раз, когда Своенравный Зверь-Поводырь наносит боевые повреждения игроку, верните землю под вашим контролем в руку ее владельца.\', \'type\': \'Существо — Зверь\', \'flavor\': \'Тактика кавалерии гоблинов — направить зверя в нужную сторону и держаться за него столько, сколько получится.\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494349&type=card\', \'language\': \'Russian\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'77e764d7-9c1a-4712-b667-cc6c916ef495\', \'multiverseId\': 494349}, \'multiverseid\': 494349}, {\'name\': \'难驭开路兽\', \'text\': \'践踏，敏捷\\n每当难驭开路兽对任一牌手造成战斗伤害时，将一个由你操控的地移回其拥有者手上。\', \'type\': \'生物 ～野兽\', \'flavor\': \'鬼怪骑兵的战术包括：给坐骑指方向，以及尽量骑背上。\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494665&type=card\', \'language\': \'Chinese Simplified\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'14fbefb9-ad70-4754-82ef-fea760b4cfe8\', \'multiverseId\': 494665}, \'multiverseid\': 494665}, {\'name\': \'難馭開路獸\', \'text\': \'踐踏，敏捷\\n每當難馭開路獸對任一玩家造成戰鬥傷害時，將一個由你操控的地移回其擁有者手上。\', \'type\': \'生物 ～野獸\', \'flavor\': \'鬼怪騎兵的戰術包括：給坐騎指方向，以及盡量騎背上。\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494981&type=card\', \'language\': \'Chinese Traditional\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'02d66463-e7d1-4056-a24f-6cbe1f4a6301\', \'multiverseId\': 494981}, \'multiverseid\': 494981}]', "[{'name': 'Abtrünnige Lotsen-Bestie', 'text': 'Verursacht Trampelschaden, Eile\\nImmer wenn die Abtrünnige Lotsen-Bestie einem Spieler Kampfschaden zufügt, bringe ein Land, das du kontrollierst, auf die Hand seines Besitzers zurück.', 'type': 'Kreatur — Bestie', 'flavor': None, 'imageUrl': 'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=495718&type=card', 'language': 'German', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'da779f80-01b5-4eff-8830-485d4a80c279', 'multiverseId': 495718}, 'multiverseid': 495718}, {'name': 'Bête-guide rétive', 'text': 'Piétinement, célérité\\nÀ chaque fois que la Bête-guide rétive inflige des blessures de combat à un joueur, renvoyez un terrain que vous contrôlez dans la main de son propriétaire.', 'type': 'Créature : bête', 'flavor': None, 'imageUrl': 'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=495793&type=card', 'language': 'French', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '03d194b6-ac3e-463a-b00c-e517d16fbc23', 'multiverseId': 495793}, 'multiverseid': 495793}, {'name': 'むら気な猛導獣', 'text': 'トランプル、速攻\\nむら気な猛導獣がプレイヤー１人に戦闘ダメージを与えるたび、あなたがコントロールしている土地１つをオーナーの手札に戻す。', 'type': 'クリーチャー — ビースト', 'flavor': None, 'imageUrl': 'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=495868&type=card', 'language': 'Japanese', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '62ffd30a-7ffb-4547-a746-690bcecfdb4b', 'multiverseId': 495868}, 'multiverseid': 495868}]", '[{\'name\': \'Adeptin der Fernsicht\', \'text\': \'Wenn die Adeptin der Fernsicht ins Spiel kommt, zieht du und ein Gegner deiner Wahl jeweils eine Karte.\', \'type\': \'Kreatur — Kor, Zauberer\', \'flavor\': \'„Ich habe jeden der Wippenden Gipfel bestiegen, ohne einen einzigen Fehltritt. Ich kann dich in Sicherheit bringen."\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=491952&type=card\', \'language\': \'German\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'0468cc25-344d-4a90-ae25-9454fbc14824\', \'multiverseId\': 491952}, \'multiverseid\': 491952}, {\'name\': \'Adepta de visión distante\', \'text\': \'Cuando la Adepta de visión distante entre al campo de batalla, el oponente objetivo y tú roban una carta.\', \'type\': \'Criatura — Hechicero kor\', \'flavor\': \'"Me he adentrado en cada uno de los Picos oscilantes y nunca he dado un paso en falso. Puedo ponerte a salvo".\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492268&type=card\', \'language\': \'Spanish\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'932db3eb-96a3-490d-9043-ff6ec1ce947a\', \'multiverseId\': 492268}, \'multiverseid\': 492268}, {\'name\': \'Experte de la clairvoyance\', \'text\': "Quand l\'Experte de la clairvoyance arrive sur le champ de bataille, un adversaire ciblé et vous piochez chacun une carte.", \'type\': \'Créature : kor et sorcier\', \'flavor\': "« J\'ai parcouru tous les Pics vacillants et je n\'ai jamais fait un pas de travers. Je peux vous conduire en lieu sûr. »", \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492584&type=card\', \'language\': \'French\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'c85f634e-02b3-42c5-b10c-057562af9e1e\', \'multiverseId\': 492584}, \'multiverseid\': 492584}, {\'name\': \'Esperta di Lungoveggenza\', \'text\': "Quando l\'Esperta di Lungoveggenza entra nel campo di battaglia, tu e un avversario bersaglio pescate una carta.", \'type\': \'Creatura — Mago Kor\', \'flavor\': \'"Ho camminato su ognuno dei Picchi Vacillanti e non ho mai fatto un passo falso. Posso portarti al sicuro."\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492900&type=card\', \'language\': \'Italian\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'4f82e710-f2f8-4df3-8b51-15708e635e5d\', \'multiverseId\': 492900}, \'multiverseid\': 492900}, {\'name\': \'遠見の達人\', \'text\': \'遠見の達人が戦場に出たとき、対戦相手１人を対象とする。あなたとそのプレイヤーはそれぞれカードを１枚引く。\', \'type\': \'クリーチャー — コー・ウィザード\', \'flavor\': \'「私はぐらつく峰をすべて歩いたけれど、踏み外したことは一度もない。あなたを安全な場所に連れていけるよ。」\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493216&type=card\', \'language\': \'Japanese\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'78a7fbf6-a614-42a6-ba7a-f7e5fee73cf5\', \'multiverseId\': 493216}, \'multiverseid\': 493216}, {\'name\': \'멀리 보는 예언자\', \'text\': \'멀리 보는 예언자가 전장에 들어올 때, 상대를 목표로 정한다. 당신과 그 상대는 각각 카드 한 장을 뽑는다.\', \'type\': \'생물 — 코르 마법사\', \'flavor\': \'"나는 불안정한 봉우리들을 한 개도 빼놓지 않고 돌아다니면서 한 번도 발을 헛디디지 않았어. 안전한 곳으로 데려다 줄게."\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493532&type=card\', \'language\': \'Korean\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'3777e8a4-f23a-4dfd-a7f7-a9dec4ed3b3b\', \'multiverseId\': 493532}, \'multiverseid\': 493532}, {\'name\': \'Adepta de Longevisão\', \'text\': \'Quando Adepta de Longevisão entra no campo de batalha, você e o oponente alvo compram um card cada.\', \'type\': \'Criatura — Kor Mago\', \'flavor\': \'"Já andei por todos os Picos Vacilantes e jamais sequer tropecei. Eu consigo levar vocês até um lugar seguro."\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493848&type=card\', \'language\': \'Portuguese (Brazil)\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'e1aaf387-02bb-4bd5-a337-41119a21574d\', \'multiverseId\': 493848}, \'multiverseid\': 493848}, {\'name\': \'Адепт Дальновидения\', \'text\': \'Когда Адепт Дальновидения выходит на поле битвы, вы и целевой оппонент берете по карте.\', \'type\': \'Существо — Кор Чародей\', \'flavor\': \'«Я побывала на каждом из Шатающихся пиков и ни разу не оступилась. Я смогу провести вас в безопасное место».\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494164&type=card\', \'language\': \'Russian\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'eb5bd2d4-71a1-4944-bb0f-70d0e8ba6c2f\', \'multiverseId\': 494164}, \'multiverseid\': 494164}, {\'name\': \'预视专家\', \'text\': \'当预视专家进战场时，你和目标对手各抓一张牌。\', \'type\': \'生物 ～寇族／法术师\', \'flavor\': \'「我曾遍足晃摇山峰每座山头，一步都未曾走错。我能带你平安下山。」\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494480&type=card\', \'language\': \'Chinese Simplified\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'99a91a51-8528-4e4a-b4a9-966019a42fc7\', \'multiverseId\': 494480}, \'multiverseid\': 494480}, {\'name\': \'預視專家\', \'text\': \'當預視專家進戰場時，你和目標對手各抽一張牌。\', \'type\': \'生物 ～寇族／魔法師\', \'flavor\': \'「我曾遍足晃搖山峰每座山頭，一步都未曾走錯。我能帶你平安下山。」\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494796&type=card\', \'language\': \'Chinese Traditional\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'f9247c7d-0fb4-41ca-a363-02404f6f908d\', \'multiverseId\': 494796}, \'multiverseid\': 494796}]', '[{\'name\': \'Agadeems Erwachen // Agadeems Unterkrypta\', \'text\': \'Bringe eine beliebige Anzahl an Kreaturenkarten deiner Wahl mit unterschiedlichen umgewandelten Manakosten von jeweils X oder weniger aus deinem Friedhof ins Spiel zurück.\\nLand\\n{T}: Erzeuge {B}.\', \'type\': \'Hexerei\', \'flavor\': \'„Jetzt ist die Stunde des Todes, kurz vor Sonnenaufgang. Wacht auf, Schläfer, und holt die Lebenden!"\\n—Vivias, Totenflüsterer\', \'faceName\': \'Agadeems Erwachen\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492039&type=card\', \'language\': \'German\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'b35b4e2e-31b1-4f7d-8120-0f3ca47cc8f1\', \'multiverseId\': 492039}, \'multiverseid\': 492039}, {\'name\': \'Despertar de Agadeem // Cripta subterránea de Agadeem\', \'text\': \'Regresa de tu cementerio al campo de batalla cualquier cantidad de cartas de criatura objetivo que tengan cada una un coste de maná convertido de X o menos diferente.\\nTierra\\n{T}: Agrega {B}.\', \'type\': \'Conjuro\', \'flavor\': \'"Es la hora de la muerte; justo antes de que amanezca. ¡Despierten, durmientes, y den caza a los vivos!".\\n—Vivias, receptáculo de brujo\', \'faceName\': \'Despertar de Agadeem\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492355&type=card\', \'language\': \'Spanish\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'f7d97a52-89c1-46dd-9ff7-0765738dc6aa\', \'multiverseId\': 492355}, \'multiverseid\': 492355}, {\'name\': "Éveil d\'Agadeem // Agadeem, la crypte inférieure", \'text\': "Renvoyez sur le champ de bataille depuis votre cimetière n\'importe quel nombre de cartes de créature ciblées ayant chacune un coût converti de mana différent inférieur ou égal à X.\\nTerrain\\n{T} : Ajoutez {B}.", \'type\': \'Rituel\', \'flavor\': "« C\'est l\'heure de la mort, juste avant l\'aube. Réveillez-vous, dormeurs, et hantez les vivants ! »\\n—Vivias, hôte sorcière", \'faceName\': "Éveil d\'Agadeem", \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492671&type=card\', \'language\': \'French\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'dbe9f14d-ce92-446d-8998-a02d27dce766\', \'multiverseId\': 492671}, \'multiverseid\': 492671}, {\'name\': \'Risveglio di Agadeem // Agadeem, la Cripta Sotterranea\', \'text\': \'Rimetti dal tuo cimitero sul campo di battaglia un qualsiasi numero di carte creatura bersaglio che hanno ciascuna un costo di mana convertito diverso pari o inferiore a X.\\nTerra\\n{T}: Aggiungi {B}.\', \'type\': \'Stregoneria\', \'flavor\': \'"Questa è l\\\'ora della morte, subito prima dell\\\'alba. Svegliatevi, dormienti, e tormentate i vivi!"\\n—Vivias, strega intermediaria\', \'faceName\': \'Risveglio di Agadeem\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492987&type=card\', \'language\': \'Italian\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'2e8c8931-d550-4573-8c8f-39b03e9c7070\', \'multiverseId\': 492987}, \'multiverseid\': 492987}, {\'name\': \'アガディームの覚醒 // 地下遺跡、アガディーム\', \'text\': \'あなたの墓地から望む枚数のクリーチャー・カードを、それぞれの点数で見たマナ・コストがＸ以下かつ互いに異なるように対象とする。それらを戦場に戻す。\\n土地\\n{T}：{B}を加える。\', \'type\': \'ソーサリー\', \'flavor\': \'「今は死の刻。もうすぐ夜明け。起きろ、眠れる者よ。生者に憑いてこい。」\\n――魔法使いの器、ヴィヴィアス\', \'faceName\': \'アガディームの覚醒\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493303&type=card\', \'language\': \'Japanese\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'10ba6544-2105-434c-afb3-9ae3ce28dc76\', \'multiverseId\': 493303}, \'multiverseid\': 493303}, {\'name\': \'아가딤의 각성 // 지하묘지, 아가딤\', \'text\': \'당신의 무덤에 있는 전환마나비용이 서로 다르며 전환마나비용이 X이하인 생물 카드들을 원하는 수만큼 목표로 정한다. 그 카드들을 전장으로 되돌린다.\\n대지\\n{T}: {B}를 추가한다.\', \'type\': \'집중마법\', \'flavor\': \'"지금은 새벽이 되기 직전인, 죽음의 시간이다. 잠든 자들아, 이제 깨어나 산 자들을 덮치거라!"\\n—마녀의 그릇, 비비아스\', \'faceName\': \'아가딤의 각성\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493619&type=card\', \'language\': \'Korean\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'f127ab1c-7209-4269-b872-2abb5f1c84ab\', \'multiverseId\': 493619}, \'multiverseid\': 493619}, {\'name\': \'Despertar de Agadeem // Agadeem, a Subcripta\', \'text\': \'Devolva de seu cemitério para o campo de batalha qualquer número de cards de criatura alvo que tenham, cada um, um custo de mana convertido igual ou inferior a X diferente.\\nTerreno\\n{T}: Adicione {B}.\', \'type\': \'Feitiço\', \'flavor\': \'"Essa é a hora da morte, logo antes do amanhecer. Despertem, adormecidos, e assombrem os vivos!"\\n— Vivias, bruxa mediúnica\', \'faceName\': \'Despertar de Agadeem\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493935&type=card\', \'language\': \'Portuguese (Brazil)\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'662e586e-a23d-4616-817b-ccd7b79d1569\', \'multiverseId\': 493935}, \'multiverseid\': 493935}, {\'name\': \'Пробуждение Агадима // Агадим, Подземный Склеп\', \'text\': \'Верните из вашего кладбища на поле битвы любое количество целевых карт существ с различными конвертированными мана-стоимостями, каждая из которых не более X.\', \'type\': \'Волшебство\', \'flavor\': \'«Перед рассветом всегда приходит час смерти. Восстаньте же, спящие, и ступайте в мир живых!»\\n— Вивиус, ведьма-вместилище\', \'faceName\': \'Пробуждение Агадима\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494251&type=card\', \'language\': \'Russian\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'c239c80d-4bc8-491d-939c-976758d75ff2\', \'multiverseId\': 494251}, \'multiverseid\': 494251}, {\'name\': \'艾格丁觉醒 // 地底墓穴艾格丁\', \'text\': \'选择任意数量目标在你坟墓场中的生物牌，其总法术力费用须各不相同且均须等于或小于X。将它们从该处移回战场。\\n地\\n{T}：加{B}。\', \'type\': \'法术\', \'flavor\': \'「现在正是拂晓之前的死亡时刻。觉醒吧，沉睡者，齐去侵扰生灵！」\\n～祟体女巫威皮斯\', \'faceName\': \'艾格丁觉醒\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494567&type=card\', \'language\': \'Chinese Simplified\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'a4a77936-11b9-4f3c-bc85-7c02024b1e0b\', \'multiverseId\': 494567}, \'multiverseid\': 494567}, {\'name\': \'艾格丁覺醒 // 地底墓穴艾格丁\', \'text\': \'選擇任意數量目標在你墳墓場中的生物牌，其總魔法力費用須各不相同且均須等於或小於X。將它們從該處移回戰場。\\n地\\n{T}：加{B}。\', \'type\': \'巫術\', \'flavor\': \'「現在正是拂曉之前的死亡時刻。覺醒吧，沉睡者，齊去侵擾生靈！」\\n～祟體女巫威皮斯\', \'faceName\': \'艾格丁覺醒\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494883&type=card\', \'language\': \'Chinese Traditional\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'fbfb2860-5d0c-4236-9475-fbb9b11e7352\', \'multiverseId\': 494883}, \'multiverseid\': 494883}]', '[{\'name\': \'Agadeems Erwachen // Agadeems Unterkrypta\', \'text\': \'Sowie Agadeems Unterkrypta ins Spiel kommt, kannst du 3 Lebenspunkte bezahlen. Falls du dies nicht tust, kommt sie getappt ins Spiel.\\n{T}: Erzeuge {B}.\\nHexerei\\n{X}{B}{B}{B}\', \'type\': \'Land\', \'flavor\': \'„Hier unter den Polyederfeldern liegen Seelen und Geheimnisse begraben."\\n—Vivias, Totenflüsterer\', \'faceName\': \'Agadeems Unterkrypta\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492039&type=card\', \'language\': \'German\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'b35b4e2e-31b1-4f7d-8120-0f3ca47cc8f1\', \'multiverseId\': 492039}, \'multiverseid\': 492039}, {\'name\': \'Despertar de Agadeem // Cripta subterránea de Agadeem\', \'text\': \'En cuanto la Cripta subterránea de Agadeem entre al campo de batalla, puedes pagar 3 vidas. Si no lo haces, entra al campo de batalla girada.\\n{T}: Agrega {B}.\\nConjuro\\n{X}{B}{B}{B}\', \'type\': \'Tierra\', \'flavor\': \'"Aquí, bajo los campos de edros, las almas y los secretos yacen sepultados".\\n—Vivias, receptáculo de brujo\', \'faceName\': \'Cripta subterránea de Agadeem\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492355&type=card\', \'language\': \'Spanish\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'f7d97a52-89c1-46dd-9ff7-0765738dc6aa\', \'multiverseId\': 492355}, \'multiverseid\': 492355}, {\'name\': "Éveil d\'Agadeem // Agadeem, la crypte inférieure", \'text\': \'Au moment où Agadeem, la crypte inférieure arrive sur le champ de bataille, vous pouvez payer 3 points de vie. Si vous ne le faites pas, elle arrive sur le champ de bataille engagée.\\n{T} : Ajoutez {B}.\\nRituel\\n{X}{B}{B}{B}\', \'type\': \'Terrain\', \'flavor\': "« Là sous les champs d\'hèdrons, sont enterrés âmes et secrets. »\\n—Vivias, hôte sorcière", \'faceName\': \'Agadeem, la crypte inférieure\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492671&type=card\', \'language\': \'French\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'dbe9f14d-ce92-446d-8998-a02d27dce766\', \'multiverseId\': 492671}, \'multiverseid\': 492671}, {\'name\': \'Risveglio di Agadeem // Agadeem, la Cripta Sotterranea\', \'text\': \'Mentre Agadeem, la Cripta Sotterranea entra nel campo di battaglia, puoi pagare 3 punti vita. Se non lo fai, entra nel campo di battaglia TAPpata.\\n{T}: Aggiungi {B}.\\nStregoneria\\n{X}{B}{B}{B}\', \'type\': \'Terra\', \'flavor\': \'"Qui, sotto i campi di edri, giacciono sepolti anime e segreti."\\n—Vivias, strega intermediaria\', \'faceName\': \'Agadeem, la Cripta Sotterranea\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492987&type=card\', \'language\': \'Italian\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'2e8c8931-d550-4573-8c8f-39b03e9c7070\', \'multiverseId\': 492987}, \'multiverseid\': 492987}, {\'name\': \'アガディームの覚醒 // 地下遺跡、アガディーム\', \'text\': \'地下遺跡、アガディームが戦場に出るに際し、あなたは３点のライフを支払ってもよい。そうしないなら、これはタップ状態で戦場に出る。\\n{T}：{B}を加える。\\nソーサリー\\n{X}{B}{B}{B}\', \'type\': \'土地\', \'flavor\': \'「面晶体原の地下には魂と秘密が葬られているのさ。」\\n――魔法使いの器、ヴィヴィアス\', \'faceName\': \'地下遺跡、アガディーム\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493303&type=card\', \'language\': \'Japanese\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'10ba6544-2105-434c-afb3-9ae3ce28dc76\', \'multiverseId\': 493303}, \'multiverseid\': 493303}, {\'name\': \'아가딤의 각성 // 지하묘지, 아가딤\', \'text\': \'지하묘지, 아가딤이 전장에 들어오면서, 당신은 생명 3점을 지불할 수 있다. 그러지 않으면, 아가딤은 탭된 채로 전장에 들어온다.\\n{T}: {B}를 추가한다.\\n집중마법\\n{X}{B}{B}{B}\', \'type\': \'대지\', \'flavor\': \'"다면체 지역의 땅 속 깊은 곳에, 영혼과 비밀들이 묻혀 있다."\\n—마녀의 그릇, 비비아스\', \'faceName\': \'지하묘지, 아가딤\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493619&type=card\', \'language\': \'Korean\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'f127ab1c-7209-4269-b872-2abb5f1c84ab\', \'multiverseId\': 493619}, \'multiverseid\': 493619}, {\'name\': \'Despertar de Agadeem // Agadeem, a Subcripta\', \'text\': \'Conforme Agadeem, a Subcripta, entra no campo de batalha, você pode pagar 3 pontos de vida. Se não fizer isso, ela entrará no campo de batalha virada.\\n{T}: Adicione {B}.\\nFeitiço\\n{X}{B}{B}{B}\', \'type\': \'Terreno\', \'flavor\': \'"Aqui, sob os campos de edro, jazem sepultos almas e segredos."\\n— Vivias, bruxa mediúnica\', \'faceName\': \'Agadeem, a Subcripta\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493935&type=card\', \'language\': \'Portuguese (Brazil)\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'662e586e-a23d-4616-817b-ccd7b79d1569\', \'multiverseId\': 493935}, \'multiverseid\': 493935}, {\'name\': \'Пробуждение Агадима // Агадим, Подземный Склеп\', \'text\': \'При выходе Агадима, Подземного Склепа на поле битвы вы можете заплатить 3 жизни. Если вы этого не делаете, он выходит на поле битвы повернутым.\\n{T}: добавьте {B}.\', \'type\': \'Земля\', \'flavor\': \'«Здесь, под эдровыми полями, погребены души и тайны».\\n— Вивиус, ведьма-вместилище\', \'faceName\': \'Агадим, Подземный Склеп\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494251&type=card\', \'language\': \'Russian\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'c239c80d-4bc8-491d-939c-976758d75ff2\', \'multiverseId\': 494251}, \'multiverseid\': 494251}, {\'name\': \'艾格丁觉醒 // 地底墓穴艾格丁\', \'text\': \'于地底墓穴艾格丁进战场时，你可以支付3点生命。如果你未如此作，则它须横置进战场。\\n{T}：加{B}。\\n法术\\n{X}{B}{B}{B}\', \'type\': \'地\', \'flavor\': \'「晶石原野之下，灵魂与秘密埋藏其间。」\\n～祟体女巫威皮斯\', \'faceName\': \'地底墓穴艾格丁\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494567&type=card\', \'language\': \'Chinese Simplified\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'a4a77936-11b9-4f3c-bc85-7c02024b1e0b\', \'multiverseId\': 494567}, \'multiverseid\': 494567}, {\'name\': \'艾格丁覺醒 // 地底墓穴艾格丁\', \'text\': \'於地底墓穴艾格丁進戰場時，你可以支付3點生命。如果你未如此作，則它須橫置進戰場。\\n{T}：加{B}。\\n巫術\\n{X}{B}{B}{B}\', \'type\': \'地\', \'flavor\': \'「晶石原野之下，靈魂與秘密埋藏其間。」\\n～祟體女巫威皮斯\', \'faceName\': \'地底墓穴艾格丁\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494883&type=card\', \'language\': \'Chinese Traditional\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'fbfb2860-5d0c-4236-9475-fbb9b11e7352\', \'multiverseId\': 494883}, \'multiverseid\': 494883}]', '[{\'name\': \'Akiri, kühne Reisende\', \'text\': \'Immer wenn du einen Spieler mit einer oder mehreren ausgerüsteten Kreaturen angreifst, ziehe eine Karte.\\n{W}: Du kannst eine Ausrüstung von einer Kreatur, die du kontrollierst, lösen. Falls du dies tust, tappe die Kreatur, und sie erhält Unzerstörbarkeit bis zum Ende des Zuges.\', \'type\': \'Legendäre Kreatur — Kor, Krieger\', \'flavor\': \'„Kein Engel versperrt uns den Aufstieg. Oben erwartet uns Emeria!"\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492187&type=card\', \'language\': \'German\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'3e991eab-6f05-46af-aab4-b03697fdb55a\', \'multiverseId\': 492187}, \'multiverseid\': 492187}, {\'name\': \'Akiri, viajera valerosa\', \'text\': \'Siempre que ataques a un jugador con una o más criaturas equipadas, roba una carta.\\n{W}: Puedes desanexar un Equipo de una criatura que controlas. Si lo haces, gira esa criatura y gana la habilidad de indestructible hasta el final del turno.\', \'type\': \'Criatura legendaria — Guerrero kor\', \'flavor\': \'"Ningún ángel nos bloquea la subida. ¡Emeria nos espera allí arriba!".\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492503&type=card\', \'language\': \'Spanish\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'025d29c1-8361-4fd6-8a3d-9a4f9c94eb3e\', \'multiverseId\': 492503}, \'multiverseid\': 492503}, {\'name\': \'Akiri, pérégrine intrépide\', \'text\': "À chaque fois que vous attaquez un joueur avec au moins une créature équipée, piochez une carte.\\n{W} : Vous pouvez détacher un équipement d\'une créature que vous contrôlez. Si vous faites ainsi, engagez cette créature et elle acquiert l\'indestructible jusqu\'à la fin du tour.", \'type\': \'Créature légendaire : kor et guerrier\', \'flavor\': \'« Aucun ange ne retient notre ascension. Là-haut, Éméria nous attend ! »\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492819&type=card\', \'language\': \'French\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'310bf67d-05e1-42ac-a941-18ff389b5237\', \'multiverseId\': 492819}, \'multiverseid\': 492819}, {\'name\': \'Akiri, Viaggiatrice Impavida\', \'text\': \'Ogniqualvolta attacchi un giocatore con una o più creature equipaggiate, pesca una carta.\\n{W}: Puoi far diventare non assegnato un Equipaggiamento che è assegnato a una creatura che controlli. Se lo fai, TAPpa quella creatura e ha indistruttibile fino alla fine del turno.\', \'type\': \'Creatura Leggendaria — Guerriero Kor\', \'flavor\': \'"Nessun angelo impedirà la nostra ascesa. Emeria ci attende lassù!"\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493135&type=card\', \'language\': \'Italian\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'5f6cbd9b-84ef-4ee4-b5b4-7944d4a95014\', \'multiverseId\': 493135}, \'multiverseid\': 493135}, {\'name\': \'恐れなき探査者、アキリ\', \'text\': \'あなたが、装備品がついているクリーチャー１体以上でプレイヤー１人を攻撃するたび、カードを１枚引く。\\n{W}：あなたはあなたがコントロールしているクリーチャー１体から装備品１つをはずしてもよい。そうしたなら、そのクリーチャーをタップする。ターン終了時まで、それは破壊不能を得る。\', \'type\': \'伝説のクリーチャー — コー・戦士\', \'flavor\': \'「私たちの上昇を阻む天使はいません。上にはエメリアが待っています！」\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493451&type=card\', \'language\': \'Japanese\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'4bd13f09-b7c2-46ea-82ec-52b2311492f8\', \'multiverseId\': 493451}, \'multiverseid\': 493451}, {\'name\': \'겁없는 여행자, 아키리\', \'text\': \'당신이 장착한 생물 한 개 이상으로 플레이어를 공격할 때마다, 카드 한 장을 뽑는다.\\n{W}: 당신은 당신이 조종하는 생물에서 장비를 분리할 수 있다. 그렇게 한다면, 그 생물을 탭하고 그 생물은 턴종료까지 무적을 얻는다.\', \'type\': \'전설적 생물 — 코르 전사\', \'flavor\': \'"우리의 등정을 막는 천사는 없다. 에메리아가 위에서 기다린다!"\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493767&type=card\', \'language\': \'Korean\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'8272dc96-9b03-43bd-b6fb-0e1d6be17c2a\', \'multiverseId\': 493767}, \'multiverseid\': 493767}, {\'name\': \'Akiri, Viajante Destemida\', \'text\': \'Toda vez que você atacar um jogador com uma ou mais criaturas equipadas, compre um card.\\n{W}: Você pode soltar um Equipamento de uma criatura que você controla. Se fizer isso, desvire aquela criatura e ela ganha indestrutível até o final do turno.\', \'type\': \'Criatura Lendária — Kor Guerreiro\', \'flavor\': \'"Nenhum anjo impede nossa ascensão. Nas alturas Emeria espera!"\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494083&type=card\', \'language\': \'Portuguese (Brazil)\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'863bd658-f671-4b2f-8947-0a050e4ce4bc\', \'multiverseId\': 494083}, \'multiverseid\': 494083}, {\'name\': \'Акири, Бесстрашная Странница\', \'text\': \'Каждый раз, когда вы атакуете игрока одним или несколькими снаряженными существами, возьмите карту.\\n{W}: вы можете открепить Снаряжение от существа под вашим контролем. Если вы это делаете, поверните то существо, и оно получает Неразрушимость до конца хода.\', \'type\': \'Легендарное Существо — Кор Воин\', \'flavor\': \'«Никакой ангел не помешает нам подняться. Эмерия ждет нас наверху!»\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494399&type=card\', \'language\': \'Russian\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'14a3f1e8-e887-4b92-af4d-5fa9b72e7d8c\', \'multiverseId\': 494399}, \'multiverseid\': 494399}, {\'name\': \'无惧旅人娅奇丽\', \'text\': \'每当你以一个或数个佩带武具的生物攻击一位牌手时，抓一张牌。\\n{W}：你可以将任一由你操控的生物上之一个武具卸装。如果你如此作，则横置该生物且它获得不灭异能直到回合结束。\', \'type\': \'传奇生物 ～寇族／战士\', \'flavor\': \'「天使也不能阻挡我们的攀爬脚步。伊美黎在上面等着我们！」\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494715&type=card\', \'language\': \'Chinese Simplified\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'e622210c-24cd-46a1-97eb-33ec38303541\', \'multiverseId\': 494715}, \'multiverseid\': 494715}, {\'name\': \'無懼旅人婭奇麗\', \'text\': \'每當你以一個或數個佩帶武具的生物攻擊一位玩家時，抽一張牌。\\n{W}：你可以將任一由你操控的生物上之一個武具卸裝。如果你如此作，則橫置該生物且它獲得不滅異能直到回合結束。\', \'type\': \'傳奇生物 ～寇族／戰士\', \'flavor\': \'「天使也不能阻擋我們的攀爬腳步。伊美黎在上面等著我們！」\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=495031&type=card\', \'language\': \'Chinese Traditional\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'0a784728-2e32-43cd-88a1-a279a64e8099\', \'multiverseId\': 495031}, \'multiverseid\': 495031}]', '[{\'name\': \'Akiri, kühne Reisende\', \'text\': \'Immer wenn du einen Spieler mit einer oder mehreren ausgerüsteten Kreaturen angreifst, ziehe eine Karte.\\n{W}: Du kannst eine Ausrüstung von einer Kreatur, die du kontrollierst, lösen. Falls du dies tust, tappe die Kreatur, und sie erhält Unzerstörbarkeit bis zum Ende des Zuges.\', \'type\': \'Legendäre Kreatur — Kor, Krieger\', \'flavor\': None, \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=495728&type=card\', \'language\': \'German\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'f7264a79-d3a2-4635-b198-e9dee7221df3\', \'multiverseId\': 495728}, \'multiverseid\': 495728}, {\'name\': \'Akiri, pérégrine intrépide\', \'text\': "À chaque fois que vous attaquez un joueur avec au moins une créature équipée, piochez une carte.\\n{W} : Vous pouvez détacher un équipement d\'une créature que vous contrôlez. Si vous faites ainsi, engagez cette créature et elle acquiert l\'indestructible jusqu\'à la fin du tour.", \'type\': \'Créature légendaire : kor et guerrier\', \'flavor\': None, \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=495803&type=card\', \'language\': \'French\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'7fde9a0e-3d66-48f8-9ad4-3fa3d8c50e8a\', \'multiverseId\': 495803}, \'multiverseid\': 495803}, {\'name\': \'恐れなき探査者、アキリ\', \'text\': \'あなたが、装備品がついているクリーチャー１体以上でプレイヤー１人を攻撃するたび、カードを１枚引く。\\n{W}：あなたはあなたがコントロールしているクリーチャー１体から装備品１つをはずしてもよい。そうしたなら、そのクリーチャーをタップする。ターン終了時まで、それは破壊不能を得る。\', \'type\': \'伝説のクリーチャー — コー・戦士\', \'flavor\': None, \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=495878&type=card\', \'language\': \'Japanese\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'d30bf8b6-45a2-40f3-8988-b723e757a8f4\', \'multiverseId\': 495878}, \'multiverseid\': 495878}]', '[{\'name\': \'Akoum-Höllenhund\', \'text\': \'Landung — Immer wenn ein Land unter deiner Kontrolle ins Spiel kommt, erhält der Akoum-Höllenhund +2/+2 bis zum Ende des Zuges.\', \'type\': \'Kreatur — Elementarwesen, Hund\', \'flavor\': \'Höllenhund-Rudel durchstreifen die Stachelfelder, schwelgen im grellen Sonnenlicht und erhellen mit ihren Flammen die Nacht.\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492088&type=card\', \'language\': \'German\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'2631c2c4-f62a-4eae-9786-60bd9d1417f8\', \'multiverseId\': 492088}, \'multiverseid\': 492088}, {\'name\': \'Perro infernal de Akoum\', \'text\': \'Aterrizaje — Siempre que una tierra entre al campo de batalla bajo tu control, el Perro infernal de Akoum obtiene +2/+2 hasta el final del turno.\', \'type\': \'Criatura — Perro elemental\', \'flavor\': \'Los perros infernales rondan por los Campospunzantes, donde disfrutan de los fuertes rayos solares e iluminan la noche con sus llamas.\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492404&type=card\', \'language\': \'Spanish\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'824a3132-772c-4016-8d4d-9f69dbc69aa7\', \'multiverseId\': 492404}, \'multiverseid\': 492404}, {\'name\': "Cerbère d\'Akoum", \'text\': "Toucheterre — À chaque fois qu\'un terrain arrive sur le champ de bataille sous votre contrôle, le Cerbère d\'Akoum gagne +2/+2 jusqu\'à la fin du tour.", \'type\': \'Créature : élémental et chien\', \'flavor\': \'Les meutes de cerbères courent les Champs de pics, se prélassent sous le soleil impétueux, et éclairent la nuit avec leurs flammes.\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=492720&type=card\', \'language\': \'French\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'b8a697fc-d3e7-4c42-aa7e-dff0a43942ee\', \'multiverseId\': 492720}, \'multiverseid\': 492720}, {\'name\': \'Segugio Infernale di Akoum\', \'text\': \'Terraferma — Ogniqualvolta una terra entra nel campo di battaglia sotto il tuo controllo, il Segugio Infernale di Akoum prende +2/+2 fino alla fine del turno.\', \'type\': \'Creatura — Canide Elementale\', \'flavor\': "Branchi di segugi infernali vagano per i Campi Aguzzi, crogiolandosi all\'impietosa luce del sole e illuminando la notte con le loro fiamme.", \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493036&type=card\', \'language\': \'Italian\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'46091031-6d97-4941-bf4e-b80fbf09b4c0\', \'multiverseId\': 493036}, \'multiverseid\': 493036}, {\'name\': \'アクームのヘルハウンド\', \'text\': \'上陸 ― 土地が１つあなたのコントロール下で戦場に出るたび、ターン終了時まで、アクームのヘルハウンドは＋２/＋２の修整を受ける。\', \'type\': \'クリーチャー — エレメンタル・犬\', \'flavor\': \'ヘルハウンドの群れが棘平原をうろついている。容赦ない日差しの下でくつろぎ、夜を自らの炎で照らしている。\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493352&type=card\', \'language\': \'Japanese\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'36709369-eee3-4901-9e76-304d1611e76f\', \'multiverseId\': 493352}, \'multiverseid\': 493352}, {\'name\': \'아쿰 지옥견\', \'text\': \'대지력 — 대지가 당신의 조종하에 전장에 들어올 때마다, 아쿰 지옥견은 턴종료까지 +2/+2를 받는다.\', \'type\': \'생물 — 정령 개\', \'flavor\': \'지옥견 무리들은 가시지대를 돌아다니며 낮에는 뜨거운 햇빛을 쬐고 밤에는 자신들의 불길로 어둠을 밝힌다.\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493668&type=card\', \'language\': \'Korean\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'98d0cd5f-c743-4994-a634-192e2ab89fc4\', \'multiverseId\': 493668}, \'multiverseid\': 493668}, {\'name\': \'Sabujo Infernal de Akoum\', \'text\': \'Aterragem — Toda vez que um terreno entra no campo de batalha sob seu controle, Sabujo Infernal de Akoum recebe +2/+2 até o final do turno.\', \'type\': \'Criatura — Elemental Cão\', \'flavor\': \'Matilhas de sabujos infernais vagam pelo Campo das Agulhas, desfrutando o sol abrasador e iluminando a noite com suas chamas.\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=493984&type=card\', \'language\': \'Portuguese (Brazil)\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'05c16c04-495d-4fa2-984a-ba5be469b139\', \'multiverseId\': 493984}, \'multiverseid\': 493984}, {\'name\': \'Акумский Цербер\', \'text\': \'Землепад — Каждый раз, когда земля выходит на поле битвы под вашим контролем, Акумский Цербер получает +2/+2 до конца хода.\', \'type\': \'Существо — Элементаль Собака\', \'flavor\': \'Стаи церберов бродят по Полям Шипов, купаясь в лучах сурового солнца, а ночь освещая своими огнями.\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494300&type=card\', \'language\': \'Russian\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'5feb9a4b-1e04-42e0-9c9b-bb2aa5313523\', \'multiverseId\': 494300}, \'multiverseid\': 494300}, {\'name\': \'阿库姆地狱犬\', \'text\': \'地落～每当一个地在你的操控下进战场时，阿库姆地狱犬得+2/+2直到回合结束。\', \'type\': \'生物 ～元素／狗\', \'flavor\': \'地狱犬群在尖岩原四处游荡，白天享受此处严酷阳光，晚间便用自身火光照亮夜空。\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494616&type=card\', \'language\': \'Chinese Simplified\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'5b1cd8ac-c032-415d-9549-04630022f0ec\', \'multiverseId\': 494616}, \'multiverseid\': 494616}, {\'name\': \'阿庫姆地獄犬\', \'text\': \'地落～每當一個地在你的操控下進戰場時，阿庫姆地獄犬得+2/+2直到回合結束。\', \'type\': \'生物 ～元素／狗\', \'flavor\': \'地獄犬群在尖岩原四處遊蕩，白天享受此處嚴酷陽光，晚間便用自身火光照亮夜空。\', \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=494932&type=card\', \'language\': \'Chinese Traditional\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'3c955cb1-8d8f-4eee-8bbd-a4a2e65a5adf\', \'multiverseId\': 494932}, \'multiverseid\': 494932}]', '[{\'name\': \'Akoum-Höllenhund\', \'text\': \'Landung — Immer wenn ein Land unter deiner Kontrolle ins Spiel kommt, erhält der Akoum-Höllenhund +2/+2 bis zum Ende des Zuges.\', \'type\': \'Kreatur — Elementarwesen, Hund\', \'flavor\': None, \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=495220&type=card\', \'language\': \'German\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'85cc1cbb-07bf-47c8-9165-3c4b33fd2115\', \'multiverseId\': 495220}, \'multiverseid\': 495220}, {\'name\': \'Perro infernal de Akoum\', \'text\': \'Aterrizaje — Siempre que una tierra entre al campo de batalla bajo tu control, el Perro infernal de Akoum obtiene +2/+2 hasta el final del turno.\', \'type\': \'Criatura — Perro elemental\', \'flavor\': None, \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=495245&type=card\', \'language\': \'Spanish\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'fcaf7d82-64cc-4f94-8d4a-7118a058705f\', \'multiverseId\': 495245}, \'multiverseid\': 495245}, {\'name\': "Cerbère d\'Akoum", \'text\': "Toucheterre — À chaque fois qu\'un terrain arrive sur le champ de bataille sous votre contrôle, le Cerbère d\'Akoum gagne +2/+2 jusqu\'à la fin du tour.", \'type\': \'Créature : élémental et chien\', \'flavor\': None, \'imageUrl\': \'http://gatherer.wizards.com/Handlers/Image.ashx?multiverseid=495270&type=card\', \'lang